writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
