{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && rg -n -i 'micro_opt|forward|decode|early|bypass|regfile|hazard|hyp-20260711-001-r' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:3:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r2s2 (regression, -2.41%): For this CoreMark front end, a committed four-entry RAS's canonical-JALR decode, stack-top target mux, and EX training state cost more than eliminating return recovery bubbles, so return prediction must stay off the fetch-critical path unless its dynamic benefit is demonstrably larger.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:4:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r3s1 (improvement, +8.89%): Resolving conditional branches in ID with EX/MEM/WB operand bypasses and a load-use interlock recovers one CoreMark mispredict slot without extending the fetch predictor's Fmax-critical lookup cone, provided the carried early-resolved bit suppresses EX's duplicate redirect.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:6:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r5s0 (regression, -23.69%): Once branches are already resolved in ID, carrying a 32-bit successor plus direction and misalignment state through ID/EX only trades EX recomputation for wider registered routing without reducing CoreMark recovery bubbles, so duplicate control logic should remain unless post-route timing proves the payload is cheaper.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:8:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r6s0 (improvement, +0.95%): Sharing a single unsigned magnitude quotient/remainder cone across DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU modestly reduces divider LUT/routing pressure while preserving RV32M sign, zero-divisor, and INT_MIN/-1 behavior through explicit result restoration.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:9:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.90%): With a two-bit BHT already in the fetch path, weakly-taken reset harms CoreMark more through cold forward/not-taken branches and aliases than it saves on first counted-loop back edges, so the weakly-not-taken cold bias is the better default.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -8.26%): Decode-resolving canonical JALR returns with bypass readiness, load-dependency, and alignment checks regresses CoreMark when the saved recovery slot on short helper returns cannot amortize the added ID-stage control/target logic, so return recovery needs a lower-cost path or stronger dynamic evidence.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:11:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r8s0 (regression, -46.02%): Replacing signed MULH/MULHSU product cones with unsigned-high-half sign corrections can severely hurt the ALU critical path because the multiplier result now feeds conditional 32-bit subtractor chains with sign/operand fanout, so arithmetic sharing must be judged post-route rather than by multiplier-cone count.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:12:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r8s1 (regression, -34.19%): A same-cycle dmem-to-EX load bypass can lose badly when its read-data extension and forwarding mux extend the dependent ALU timing cone, so removing a CoreMark load-use bubble requires post-route proof that the memory-to-EX path is faster than the saved cycle.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:13:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r8s2 (improvement, +1.43%): After operand-ready conditional branches redirect in ID, removing the BHT's counter lookup, branch-legality decode, target adder, and direction mux from the fetch-to-PC path can outperform its remaining load-dependent-branch benefit while retaining immediate direct-JAL prediction.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:14:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r9s0 (regression, -61.98%): Splitting a live FPGA-visible 64-bit counter can regress badly when the low-word terminal-count compare and conditional high-word increment add a wide control path that outweighs the shorter common carry chain, so counter decomposition needs post-route evidence rather than carry-width intuition.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:15:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.97%): Even a bypass-free `jalr x0, x1, 0` decode redirect regresses CoreMark when x1-pending comparisons, target alignment gating, and the ID early-redirect selection add control/routing cost that common return bubbles cannot amortize, so canonical-return recovery should remain in EX unless its decode path is demonstrably cheaper post-route.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:16:  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r10s0 (regression, -58.18%): Registering the entire RVFI retirement payload can lose badly on this FPGA because the added wide bundle of flip-flops and routing outweighs any relief from removing MEM/WB and writeback-mux fanout, so high-fanout observability logic needs post-route validation before adding a full-width pipeline stage.\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-7155d3c\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T12:43:42.657419Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Prune dead EX branch payload\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and\\ntheir EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on\\nduplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint\\nwhile preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller\\nEX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 302.55, \"delta_pct\": 6.98, \"vs_baseline\": 6.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative divide execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}]