cted using a forwarded value while retaining a\\nstale operand, which broke the formal register check. Load-dependent and\\nmisaligned JALRs remain on the precise EX path, and a resolved-in-ID flag\\nsuppresses only the duplicate EX redirect.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID marker while retaining the existing compact payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply the established EX/MEM/WB bypass priority to legal JALR target calculation and latch the selected operands, not raw regfile values, into ID/EX for JALR.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the control-resolved-in-ID marker to suppress only duplicate JALR recovery while preserving link writeback, misalignment trapping, and RVFI operand reporting.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the validated decode-stage JALR redirect through the existing redirect-priority path without adding predictor lookup logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve load-use and dmem-stall precedence so a JALR dependent on a load remains unresolved until its operand is forwardable.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add independent, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned JALR cases that check redirect depth, link writeback, RVFI rs1 data, register state, and retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID marker while retaining the existing compact payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Apply the established EX/MEM/WB bypass priority to legal JALR target calculation and latch the selected operands, not raw regfile values, into ID/EX for JALR.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the control-resolved-in-ID marker to suppress only duplicate JALR recovery while preserving link writeback, misalignment trapping, and RVFI operand reporting.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the validated decode-stage JALR redirect through the existing redirect-priority path without adding predictor lookup logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve load-use and dmem-stall precedence so a JALR dependent on a load remains unresolved until its operand is forwardable.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add independent, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned JALR cases that check redirect depth, link writeback, RVFI rs1 data, register state, and retirement order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\n:10:42 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:50 (50)\\nSBY 14:10:42 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 14:10:42 [insn_sw_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 14:10:42 [insn_sw_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:00  waiting for solver (1 minute)\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:00  Checking assertions in step 20..\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:00  Status: passed\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:01 (61)\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:56 (56)\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 14:10:50 [insn_xor_ch0] DONE (P