{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i 'micro_opt|forward|load.use|hazard|bypass|branch' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): An iterative EX divider must preserve the pipeline's valid/retirement progress contract while it holds ID/EX; freezing around a multicycle response can make DIV/REM formal assumptions unreachable and fail liveness even when unrelated instructions pass.\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (improvement, +11.79%): A compact PC-indexed two-bit BHT that predicts direct B-immediate targets and JALs removes the repeated two-slot EX recovery bubbles in CoreMark's short counted loops, provided EX compares resolved and carried predicted next PCs before flushing.\n1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-7155d3c\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T12:43:42.657419Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Prune dead EX branch payload\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and\\ntheir EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on\\nduplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint\\nwhile preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller\\nEX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 302.55, \"delta_pct\": 6.98, \"vs_baseline\": 6.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\n3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative divide execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\