{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0.yaml && (command -v ruby >/dev/null && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0.yaml || true)\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Static backward branch fast path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The 16-entry dynamic BHT substantially improved CoreMark by avoiding\n  recovery bubbles in counted loops, but its indexed counter-array read and\n  update state now sit in the fetch-critical logic and reduced placed Fmax.\n  CoreMark's dominant loop-closing conditional branches are direct backward\n  B-type branches whose usual direction is predictable from the immediate.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the PC-indexed two-bit counter lookup with a stateless\n  backward-taken/forward-not-taken policy for validated conditional branches,\n  while retaining direct-JAL target prediction and existing EX comparison\n  recovery. A negative B-immediate predicts its direct target; forward\n  branches stay sequential. This removes the BHT flops, index mux, reset\n  fanout, and training cone from fetch, avoids the first-iteration loop miss,\n  and should preserve nearly all CoreMark loop IPC at a higher Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Replace the indexed saturating-counter table and training state with a combinational validated-B-type backward-taken predictor, while keeping direct-JAL prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Remove obsolete execute-to-predictor branch-training connections and retain the predicted-next-PC lookup and recovery wiring.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove branch-training outputs that are no longer needed, preserving resolved-next-PC computation and misprediction redirect behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed checks for backward conditional prediction, forward sequential prediction, loop exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\", \"title\"=>\"Static backward branch fast path\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The 16-entry dynamic BHT substantially improved CoreMark by avoiding\\nrecovery bubbles in counted loops, but its indexed counter-array read and\\nupdate state now sit in the fetch-critical logic and reduced placed Fmax.\\nCoreMark's dominant loop-closing conditional branches are direct backward\\nB-type branches whose usual direction is predictable from the immediate.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Replace the PC-indexed two-bit counter lookup with a stateless\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken policy for validated conditional branches,\\nwhile retaining direct-JAL target prediction and existing EX comparison\\nrecovery. A negative B-immediate predicts its direct target; forward\\nbranches stay sequential. This removes the BHT flops, index mux, reset\\nfanout, and training cone from fetch, avoids the first-iteration loop miss,\\nand should preserve nearly all CoreMark loop IPC at a higher Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>5, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Replace the indexed saturating-counter table and training state with a combinational validated-B-type backward-taken predictor, while keeping direct-JAL prediction.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Remove obsolete execute-to-predictor branch-training connections and retain the predicted-next-PC lookup and recovery wiring.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Remove branch-training outputs that are no longer needed, preserving resolved-next-PC computation and misprediction redirect behavior.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\"=>\"Add directed checks for backward conditional prediction, forward sequential prediction, loop exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
