{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r6s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r6s0.yaml\\\")' && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Shared magnitude divide datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\n  remainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\n  selectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\n  even though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the four DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with a shared magnitude\n  quotient/remainder datapath: derive operand magnitudes only for signed\n  operations, perform one unsigned divide and modulo pair, and restore the\n  quotient or remainder sign according to RV32M rules. Keep explicit\n  divide-by-zero behavior and retain the magnitude-based INT_MIN/-1 results.\n  This halves the divider-class operator count without changing latency,\n  forwarding, retirement, or the fetch-critical predictor path, so it should\n  improve Tang Nano placement and Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU vectors across signedness boundaries, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and randomized values to validate the shared datapath.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\", \"title\"=>\"Shared magnitude divide datapath\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\\nremainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\\nselectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\\neven though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Replace the four DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with a shared magnitude\\nquotient/remainder datapath: derive operand magnitudes only for signed\\noperations, perform one unsigned divide and modulo pair, and restore the\\nquotient or remainder sign according to RV32M rules. Keep explicit\\ndivide-by-zero behavior and retain the magnitude-based INT_MIN/-1 results.\\nThis halves the divider-class operator count without changing latency,\\nforwarding, retirement, or the fetch-critical predictor path, so it should\\nimprove Tang Nano placement and Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\"=>\"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU vectors across signedness boundaries, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and randomized values to validate the shared datapath.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
