{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\\\") | {id,title,outcome,delta_pct,motivation,hypothesis,changes,error,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\",\"title\":\"Prune dead EX branch payload\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":6.98,\"motivation\":\"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and\\ntheir EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on\\nduplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint\\nwhile preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller\\nEX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}],\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\",\"title\":\"Decode-aware load-use interlock\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"motivation\":\"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the\\nload-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads\\nthe matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store,\\nJALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in\\nCoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, or retirement semantics.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/decoder.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must still interlock and retire correctly.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/decoder.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must still interlock and retire correctly.\"}],\"error\":\"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\nBY 10:07:48 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:24 (24)\\nSBY 10:07:48 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:22 (22)\\nSBY 10:07:48 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 10:07:48 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 10:07:48 [insn_sub_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 10:07:50 [insn_srl_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:36  Checking assertions in step 20..\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:37  Status: passed\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:37 (37)\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:34 (34)\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 10:07:51 [insn_srl_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 10:05:53 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 10:05:53 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 14..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 15..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 16..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 17..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 18..\\nSBY 10:05:54 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 19..\\n