gs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-001-r2s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-51234/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\",\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Static backward branch fast path\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":0.0,\"motivation\":\"The 16-entry dynamic BHT substantially improved CoreMark by avoiding\\nrecovery bubbles in counted loops, but its indexed counter-array read and\\nupdate state now sit in the fetch-critical logic and reduced placed Fmax.\\nCoreMark's dominant loop-closing conditional branches are direct backward\\nB-type branches whose usual direction is predictable from the immediate.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The 16-entry dynamic BHT substantially improved CoreMark by avoiding\\nrecovery bubbles in counted loops, but its indexed counter-array read and\\nupdate state now sit in the fetch-critical logic and reduced placed Fmax.\\nCoreMark's dominant loop-closing conditional branches are direct backward\\nB-type branches whose usual direction is predictable from the immediate.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the PC-indexed two-bit counter lookup with a stateless\\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken policy for validated conditional branches,\\nwhile retaining direct-JAL target prediction and existing EX comparison\\nrecovery. A negative B-immediate predicts its direct target; forward\\nbranches stay sequential. This removes the BHT flops, index mux, reset\\nfanout, and training cone from fetch, avoids the first-iteration loop miss,\\nand should preserve nearly all CoreMark loop IPC at a higher Fmax.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the indexed saturating-counter table and training state with a combinational validated-B-type backward-taken predictor, while keeping direct-JAL prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove obsolete execute-to-predictor branch-training connections and retain the predicted-next-PC lookup and recovery wiring.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove branch-training outputs that are no longer needed, preserving resolved-next-PC computation and misprediction redirect behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed checks for backward conditional prediction, forward sequential prediction, loop exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the indexed saturating-counter table and training state with a combinational validated-B-type backward-taken predictor, while keeping direct-JAL prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove obsolete execute-to-predictor branch-training connections and retain the predicted-next-PC lookup and recovery wiring.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove branch-training outputs that are no longer needed, preserving resolved-next-PC computation and misprediction redirect behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add directed checks for backward conditional prediction, forward sequential prediction, loop exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}],\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\",\"title\":\"Single narrow RV32M multiplier\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-6.54,\"motivation\":\"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Select operand extension from the decoded multiply operation and compute one\\nsigned 33-by-33 product, selecting its low half for MUL and bits [63:32]\\nfor MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. This preserves all RV32M signedness semantics\\nwhile eliminating two parallel multipliers and avoiding the accidental\\n64-bit operand expansion. The smaller arithmetic fabric should reduce\\nplacement pressure and improve Fmax without adding latency or changing IPC.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_alu.py\",\"description\":\"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_alu.py\",\"description\":\"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\"}],\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
