tage later in EX. That leaves the predictor using\\nstale counter state for the next fetches after a direction change, despite\\nthe correct branch outcome already being available without another ALU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches are now resolved with current operands in ID, but the\\nBHT is still updated one stage later in EX. That leaves the predictor using\\nstale counter state for the next fetches after a direction change, despite\\nthe correct branch outcome already being available without another ALU.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Train the existing two-bit BHT directly from the validated, operand-ready\\ndecode-stage branch result and remove the redundant EX-to-predictor training\\npath. This advances counter updates by one cycle without changing BHT size,\\nindexing, reset policy, direct-target generation, or the fetch lookup cone.\\nIt should reduce short-loop and closely spaced alias recovery bubbles while\\npreserving the successful ID-stage redirect and EX fallback behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a valid, non-stalled decode-stage branch-training event carrying the resolved branch PC and direction, gated until operands are forwardable and the instruction is legal.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-stage branch training to the existing predictor and remove the superseded EX-stage training connections while retaining all redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove redundant BHT training outputs; keep branch execution, misalignment traps, resolved pc_next, and EX recovery for branches not resolved in ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the earlier committed decode-stage training event without altering the sixteen-entry counter lookup, direct JAL prediction, or fetch-critical prediction selection.\