ctor\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage baseline resolves every conditional branch and JAL in EX,\\nflushing two younger instructions whenever control flow changes. CoreMark\\nspends substantial time in short counted loops, so correctly predicting\\ntheir backward branches can recover those repeated front-end bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage baseline resolves every conditional branch and JAL in EX,\\nflushing two younger instructions whenever control flow changes. CoreMark\\nspends substantial time in short counted loops, so correctly predicting\\ntheir backward branches can recover those repeated front-end bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit counter predictor that recognizes validated B-type branches and direct JAL targets, and trains on resolved conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and execute pipeline bundles with the predicted next-PC metadata needed for precise misprediction recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor direction and direct targets to select the speculative next PC while preserving reset, stall, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control flow against the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction, while exposing branch-training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, execute-stage training, and misprediction recovery through the existing hazard and fetch controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the execute redirect input as a misprediction recovery request so only incorrectly predicted paths are flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correctly predicted loop branches, counter training and saturation, JAL prediction, and branch misprediction recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit counter predictor that recognizes validated B-type branches and direct JAL targets, and trains on resolved conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and execute pipeline bundles with the predicted next-PC metadata needed for precise misprediction recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor direction and direct targets to select the speculative next PC while preserving reset, stall, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control flow against the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction, while exposing branch-training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, execute-stage training, and misprediction recovery through the existing hazard and fetch controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the execute redirect input as a misprediction recovery request so only incorrectly predicted paths are flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correctly predicted loop branches, counter training and saturation, JAL prediction, and branch misprediction recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 316.16, \"delta_pct\": 11.79, \"vs_baseline\": 11.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4219411, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10561, \"ff\": 1939, \"seeds\": [137.8, 133.4, 129.63], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T12:56:46.486928Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (improvement, +11.79%): A compact PC-indexed two-bit BHT that predicts direct B-immediate targets and JALs removes the repeated two-slot EX recovery bubbles in CoreMark's short counted loops, provided EX compares resolved and carried predicted next PCs before flushing.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Decode-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the\\nload-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads\\nthe matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store,\\nJALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in\\nCoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, or retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must still interlock and retire correctly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load ca