rm-up cost hurts Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current BHT initializes every counter as weakly not taken, so each\\nnewly encountered counted-loop back edge pays a recovery before the table\\nlearns its overwhelmingly taken steady-state direction. CoreMark repeatedly\\nenters compact loops, while the prior BTFNT fallback showed that adding\\nlookup logic to address this warm-up cost hurts Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Initialize the existing sixteen two-bit BHT counters to weakly taken\\n(2'b10) instead of weakly not taken (2'b01). This removes the first-taken\\nmisprediction for cold loop back edges with no new state, muxing, PC hash,\\nor fetch-path logic. A first not-taken forward branch still trains the same\\ncounter to weakly not taken after one recovery, retaining normal dynamic\\nbehavior and existing decode-stage training semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Change BHT reset initialization to weakly taken while retaining the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Change BHT reset initialization to weakly taken while retaining the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\",