corrections:\\nsubtract b when rs1 is negative and subtract a when rs2 is negative, with\\nonly the applicable term used for MULHSU. This removes the two wide signed\\nproduct cones without changing EX latency, forwarding, retirement, or the\\nproven divide datapath. It should reduce LUT/routing pressure and raise Fmax\\nwhile preserving CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace mul_ss and mul_su with high-half sign-correction logic driven from the existing unsigned 32 by 32 product; preserve all RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and divide/remainder behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact boundary and randomized MULH/MULHSU vectors covering each operand sign combination, including INT_MIN and all-ones unsigned operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace mul_ss and mul_su with high-half sign-correction logic driven from the existing unsigned 32 by 32 product; preserve all RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and divide/remainder behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact boundary and randomized MULH/MULHSU vectors covering each operand sign combination, including INT_MIN and all-ones unsigned operands.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 188.19, \"delta_pct\": -46.02, \"vs_baseline\": -33.46, \"fmax_mhz\": 78.07, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8166, \"ff\": 1931, \"seeds\": [78.47, 78.07, 73.76], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:29:10.151064Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r8s0 (regression, -46.02%): Replacing signed MULH/MULHSU product cones with unsigned-high-half sign correction