dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 302.55, \"delta_pct\": 6.98, \"vs_baseline\": 6.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:11:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Single narrow RV32M multiplier\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Select operand extension from the decoded multiply operation and compute one\\nsigned 33-by-33 product, selecting its low half for MUL and bits [63:32]\\nfor MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. This preserves all RV32M signedness semantics\\nwhile eliminating two parallel multipliers and avoiding the accidental\\n64-bit operand expansion. The smaller arithmetic fabric should reduce\\nplacement pressure and improve Fmax without adding latency or changing IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 321.75, \"delta_pct\": -6.54, \"vs_baseline\": 13.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.48, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10988, \"ff\": 1931, \"seeds\": [122.44, 133.48, 141.48], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:03:34.473639Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 4}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:14:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Authoritative decode branch resolution\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode stage already compares fully bypassed branch operands and\\ncomputes the direct successor, yet EX repeats the branch comparison and\\ntarget calculation before registering the same RVFI pc_wdata result. This\\nduplicate conditional-control cone adds LUTs and routing to the EX/MEM\\nendpoint after the successful early-resolution optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode stage already compares fully bypassed branch operands and\\ncomputes the direct successor, yet EX repeats the branch comparison and\\ntarget calculation before registering the same RVFI pc_wdata result. This\\nduplicate conditional-control cone adds LUTs and routing to the EX/MEM\\nendpoint after the successful early-resolution optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the decode-stage branch decision authoritative for every legal\\nconditional branch once its operands are ready. Carry the resolved taken\\nbit, successor, and target-misalignment fault state through ID/EX so EX\\nselects the recorded result, trains the BHT from the recorded direction,\\nand preserves precise illegal/trap behavior without recomputing a branch\\ncomparator or PC-plus-immediate adder. This should shorten the EX control\\npath while retaining the existing load interlock and recovery semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with decode-resolved branch direction, successor, and misalignment metadata; remove obsolete EX/MEM branch-only payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the fully bypassed conditional-branch outcome for legal ready branches, including the taken misaligned-target fault condition, alongside the existing early redirect result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace duplicated conditional-branch comparison and target generation with the carried decode result, preserving redirect priority, trap conversion, RVFI pc_wdata, and BHT training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update EX/MEM bundle assumptions after removal of branch-only fields that are no longer consumed downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases for bypassed taken and not-taken branches, load-dependent branch interlocks, misaligned taken targets, predictor training, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with decode-resolved branch direction, successor, and misalignment metadata; remove obsolete EX/MEM branch-only payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the fully bypassed conditional-branch outcome for legal ready branches, including the taken misaligned-target fault condition, alongside the existing early redirect result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace duplicated conditional-branch comparison and target generation with the carried decode result, preserving redirect priority, trap conversion, RVFI pc_wdata, and BHT training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update EX/MEM bundle assumptions after removal of branch-only fields that are no longer consumed downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases for bypassed taken and not-taken branches, load-dependent branch interlocks, misaligned taken targets, predictor training, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 262.72, \"delta_pct\": -23.69, \"vs_baseline\": -7.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 108.99, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10442, \"ff\": 1958, \"seeds\": [108.99, 110.06, 103.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:37:44.605648Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r5s0 (regression, -23.69%): Once branches are already resolved in ID, carrying a 32-bit successor plus direction and misalignment state through ID/EX only trades EX recomputation for wider registered routing without reducing CoreMark recovery bubbles, so duplicate control logic should remain unless post-route timing proves the payload is cheaper.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"JAL-only fetch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID with bypassing, so a sequential\\nconditional fetch can usually be repaired at the same edge without an\\nextra decode bubble. The BHT still places a counter-array mux, branch\\nlegality decode, immediate-target adder, and direction mux on every\\ninstruction-fetch path. Direct JALs cannot use the ID branch mechanism\\nand remain worth predicting at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID with bypassing, so a sequential\\nconditional fetch can usually be repaired at the same edge without an\\nextra decode bubble. The BHT still places a counter-array mux, branch\\nlegality decode, immediate-target adder, and direction mux on every\\ninstruction-fetch path. Direct JALs cannot use the ID branch mechanism\\nand remain worth predicting at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the conditional two-bit BHT prediction with a minimal direct-JAL\\nfetch predictor: JAL is still sent immediately to its encoded target, but\\nconditional branches always fetch PC+4 and rely on the established\\noperand-ready ID redirect for taken outcomes. Remove BHT state and its\\ndecode-stage training interface. This trades the limited remaining benefit\\nof speculative conditional direction (principally load-dependent branches)\\nfor a shorter, lower-fanout fetch-to-PC path while retaining bubble-free\\ndirect calls and jumps.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the conditional BHT counter array, PC-index lookup, and training ports; retain only validated direct-JAL target prediction with sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete decode-stage BHT training wires and instantiate the simplified JAL-only predictor while preserving predicted-next-PC recovery plumbing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch-training outputs and keep existing operand-ready conditional branch comparison and early redirect behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain direct-JAL speculation and verify that sequential conditional fetch plus ID redirect has the required redirect and stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Replace counter-state tests with direct-JAL and sequential-conditional lookup tests, including reserved branch encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add taken and not-taken conditional branch cases, including forwarded and load-dependent operands, to verify decode recovery, RVFI PC order, and direct-JAL fetch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the conditional BHT counter array, PC-index lookup, and training ports; retain only validated direct-JAL target prediction with sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete decode-stage BHT training wires and instantiate the simplified JAL-only predictor while preserving predicted-next-PC recovery plumbing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch-training outputs and keep existing operand-ready conditional branch comparison and early redirect behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain direct-JAL speculation and verify that sequential conditional fetch plus ID redirect has the required redirect and stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Replace counter-state tests with direct-JAL and sequential-conditional lookup tests, including reserved branch encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add taken and not-taken conditional branch cases, including forwarded and load-dependent operands, to verify decode recovery, RVFI PC order, and direct-JAL fetch behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 353.6, \"delta_pct\": 1.43, \"vs_baseline\": 25.03, \"fmax_mhz\": 146.69, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8082, \"ff\": 1900, \"seeds\": [147.1, 146.69, 145.29], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:34:38.774222Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r8s2 (improvement, +1.43%): After operand-ready conditional branches redirect in ID, removing the BHT's counter lookup, branch-legality decode, target adder, and direction mux from the fetch-to-PC path can outperform its remaining load-dependent-branch benefit while retaining immediate direct-JAL prediction.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Split RVFI retirement-order counter\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The single-issue core increments a live 64-bit RVFI order register at every\\nretirement. The FPGA wrapper XOR-reduces RVFI outputs into its LED, so this\\ncounter and its wide carry path remain in the placed design even though it\\ndoes not affect architectural execution or CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The single-issue core increments a live 64-bit RVFI order register at every\\nretirement. The FPGA wrapper XOR-reduces RVFI outputs into its LED, so this\\ncounter and its wide carry path remain in the placed design even though it\\ndoes not affect architectural execution or CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the monolithic 64-bit retirement-order incrementer with a low and\\nhigh 32-bit counter. Increment the low word on every valid retirement and\\nincrement the high word only when the low word wraps; concatenate the words\\nfor io_rvfi_order_0. This preserves exact modulo-2^64 strictly increasing\\nRVFI order semantics while shortening the common registered carry chain\\nfrom 64 to 32 bits, reducing routing pressure without changing IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the 64-bit rvfi_order_q incrementer with carry-coupled 32-bit low/high registers and concatenate them on the RVFI channel-0 order output.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add retirement-order checks across ordinary valid/bubble cycles and a forced low-word wrap to confirm exact monotonic 64-bit RVFI ordering.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the 64-bit rvfi_order_q incrementer with carry-coupled 32-bit low/high registers and concatenate them on the RVFI channel-0 order output.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add retirement-order checks across ordinary valid/bubble cycles and a forced low-word wrap to confirm exact monotonic 64-bit RVFI ordering.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 134.43, \"delta_pct\": -61.98, \"vs_baseline\": -52.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 55.77, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7946, \"ff\": 1888, \"seeds\": [53.91, 55.77, 58.69], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:43:57.973602Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r9s0 (regression, -61.98%): Splitting a live FPGA-visible 64-bit counter can regress badly when the low-word terminal-count compare and conditional high-word increment add a wide control path that outweighs the shorter common carry chain, so counter decomposition needs post-route evidence rather than carry-width intuition.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Clean-register return fast predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The JAL-only fetch path has restored Fmax, while conditional branches already\\nrecover in decode. Canonical returns remain a recurring two-slot EX recovery,\\nbut the previous general decode-return path lost heavily to its bypass and\\ntarget-calculation logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The JAL-only fetch path has restored Fmax, while conditional branches already\\nrecover in decode. Canonical returns remain a recurring two-slot EX recovery,\\nbut the previous general decode-return path lost heavily to its bypass and\\ntarget-calculation logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a conservative decode-stage fast path only for the exact canonical return\\nencoding `jalr x0, x1, 0` when no older EX or MEM writer targets x1. Its target\\nis the clean regfile x1 value with bit zero cleared, so this path needs neither\\noperand-bypass muxes nor a 32-bit add. If x1 is pending, the target is\\nmisaligned, or the pipeline is stalled, retain normal EX-stage JALR recovery\\nand trap behavior. This can recover common leaf/helper returns without adding\\nstate or lengthening the fetch predictor cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-resolved canonical return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only jalr x0,x1,0; conservatively require x1 not to be pending in EX or MEM, form the target as the aligned clean regfile value, and issue a decode redirect only for an aligned capturable return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried return-resolved marker to avoid duplicate recovery while retaining full JALR target, link, forwarding, and misalignment-trap behavior for every other case.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow decode return redirect through the existing older-EX redirect priority without changing the JAL-only fetch predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add clean-register canonical-return, pending-x1 fallback, and misaligned-return tests that check redirect timing, RVFI PC/order, link semantics, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-res