 branch and JAL in EX,\\nflushing two younger instructions whenever control flow changes. CoreMark\\nspends substantial time in short counted loops, so correctly predicting\\ntheir backward branches can recover those repeated front-end bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit counter predictor that recognizes validated B-type branches and direct JAL targets, and trains on resolved conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and execute pipeline bundles with the predicted next-PC metadata needed for precise misprediction recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor direction and direct targets to select the speculative next PC while preserving reset, stall, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control flow against the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction, while exposing branch-training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, execute-stage training, and misprediction recovery through the existing hazard and fetch controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the execute redirect input as a misprediction recovery request so only incorrectly predicted paths are flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correctly predicted loop branches, counter training and saturation, JAL prediction, and branch misprediction recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit counter predictor that recognizes validated B-type branches and direct JAL targets, and trains on resolved conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and execute pipeline bundles with the predicted next-PC metadata needed for precise misprediction recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor direction and direct targets to select the speculative next PC while preserving reset, stall, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control flow against the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction, while exposing branch-training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, execute-stage training, and misprediction recovery through the existing hazard and fetch controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat the execute redirect input as a misprediction recovery request so only incorrectly predicted paths are flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for correctly predicted loop branches, counter training and saturation, JAL prediction, and branch misprediction recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 316.16, \"delta_pct\": 11.79, \"vs_baseline\": 11.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4219411, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10561, \"ff\": 1939, \"seeds\": [137.8, 133.4, 129.63], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": 