ement\", \"fitness\": 316.16, \"delta_pct\": 11.79, \"vs_baseline\": 11.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4219411, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10561, \"ff\": 1939, \"seeds\": [137.8, 133.4, 129.63], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T12:56:46.486928Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (improvement, +11.79%): A compact PC-indexed two-bit BHT that predicts direct B-immediate targets and JALs removes the repeated two-slot EX recovery bubbles in CoreMark's short counted loops, provided EX compares resolved and carried predicted next PCs before flushing.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Decode-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the\\nload-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads\\nthe matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store,\\nJALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in\\nCoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, or retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must still interlock and retire correctly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must s