nd broke liveness.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace only the real divide/remainder ALU path with an eight-cycle radix-4\\\\niterative unit. A precise EX interlock will accept each divide exactly once,\\\\nallow older MEM/WB work to drain, retain the DIV payload while busy, and\\\\nadvance one normal EX/MEM result on the fixed completion cycle. Eight cycles\\\\nkeeps total fetch-to-retire latency within the existing 20-step formal depth,\\\\nwhile removing the large combinational divider from the ordinary EX critical\\\\npath. MUL remains combinational and the ALTOPS behavior remains equivalent\\\\nfor formal checks.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU selection from the normal EX ALU while retaining the formal ALTOPS mapping.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add an eight-cycle radix-4 signed/unsigned divide unit with quotient/remainder selection and exact RV32M divide-by-zero and overflow handling.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Dispatch divide-class operations once, preserve their ID/EX payload during the fixed-latency operation, and emit exactly one completed EX/MEM entry.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a divider-busy interlock that freezes younger stages without suppressing older retirement or duplicate transactions.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire divider request, response, and busy state through the in-order pipeline and existing memory-stall priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Exercise exact quotient and remainder results, signed corner cases, and divide-by-zero through the bounded execution path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"descrip