h0] summary: counterexample trace: insn_div_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\\\nSBY 10:16:42 [insn_div_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_177_115 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:177.7-177.40 step 20\\\\nSBY 10:16:42 [insn_div_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\\\n\\\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r2s1/formal/last_run-66039.log\\\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r2s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-66039/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 2}\\n7:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-003-r2s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Committed return-stack JALR predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current BHT eliminates the repeated recovery bubbles for direct branches\\\\nand JALs, but every function return remains an unpredicted JALR. CoreMark's\\\\nsmall routines execute many call and return pairs, making return recovery a\\\\nconcentrated remaining front-end cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current BHT eliminates the repeated recovery bubbles for direct branches\\\\nand JALs, but every function return remains an unpredicted JALR. CoreMark's\\\\nsmall routines execute many call and return pairs, making return recovery a\\\\nconcentrated remaining front-end cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Extend the existing direct predictor with a tiny committed return-address\\\\nstack. Detect canonical RV32 calls and returns in fetch: predict a JALR\\\\nreturn through the stack top, while EX pushes PC+4 for resolved calls and\\\\npops only resolved canonical returns. Keeping updates at resolution avoids\\\\ncorrupting predictor state on a mispredicted speculative path, and avoids\\\\nthe tags, target RAM, and lookup delay of a general indirect BTB.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a shallow committed return-address stack, canonical JAL/JALR call and return recognition, resolved-call push/pop training, and stack-top prediction for returns while retaining the BHT behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose resolved canonical call and return events to train the return stack, gated with valid, non-stalled execution and existing trap handling.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire execute-stage return-stack training into the predictor and preserve the existing predicted-next-PC and recovery path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed nested-call and return tests, including return prediction, stack push/pop ordering, empty-stack sequential fallback, and wrong-path recovery.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a shallow committed return-address stack, canonical JAL/JALR call and return recognition, resolved-call push/pop training, and stack-top prediction for returns while retaining the BHT behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose resolved canonical call and return events to train the return stack, gated with valid, non-stalled execution and existing trap handling.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire execute-stage return-stack training into the predictor and preserve the existing predicted-next-PC and recovery path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed nested-call and return tests, including return prediction, stack push/pop ordering, empty-stack sequential fallback, and wrong-path recovery.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 308.55, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -2.41, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 9.1, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 129.72, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4204229, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10293, \\\"ff\\\": 2059, \\\"seeds\\\": [129.72, 119.05, 133.85], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T13:21:10.218272Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 2, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r2s2 (regression, -2.41%): For this CoreMark front end, a committed four-entry RAS's canonical-JALR decode, stack-top target mux, and EX training state cost more than eliminating return recovery bubbles, so return prediction must stay off the fetch-critical path unless its dynamic benefit is demonstrably larger.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r1s0.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r1s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r2s0.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r2s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r3s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r1s1.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r1s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r2s1.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r2s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r3s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r1s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r1s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r2s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r2s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r3s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0.yaml\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r3s2.yaml\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\nid: hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Static backward branch fast path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The 16-entry dynamic BHT substantially improved CoreMark by avoiding\n  recovery bubbles in counted loops, but its indexed counter-array read and\n  update state now sit in the fetch-critical logic and reduced placed Fmax.\n  CoreMark's dominant loop-closing conditional branches are direct backward\n  B-type branches whose usual direction is predictable from the immediate.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the PC-indexed two-bit counter lookup with a stateless\n  backward-taken/forward-not-taken policy for validated conditional branches,\n  while retaining direct-JAL target prediction and existing EX comparison\n  recovery. A negative B-immediate predicts its direct target; forward\n  branches stay sequential. This removes the BHT flops, index mux, reset\n  fanout, and training cone from fetch, avoids the first-iteration loop miss,\n  and should preserve nearly all CoreMark loop IPC at a higher Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Replace the indexed saturating-counter table and training state with a combinational validated-B-type backward-taken predictor, while keeping direct-JAL prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Remove obsolete execute-to-predictor branch-training connections and retain the predicted-next-PC lookup and recovery wiring.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove branch-training outputs that are no longer needed, preserving resolved-next-PC computation and misprediction redirect behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed checks for backward conditional prediction, forward sequential prediction, loop exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"\nid: hyp-20260711-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Cold-start BTFNT branch fallback\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current two-bit BHT is initialized weakly not taken, so every cold\n  backward loop branch incurs an avoidable EX recovery before it trains.\n  CoreMark repeatedly enters short counted loops, making this warm-up cost\n  visible even after the main BHT improvement.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one validity bit per existing BHT entry and use static backward-taken,\n  forward-not-taken prediction only while that entry is untrained. On the\n  first resolved branch, mark the entry valid and retain the present two-bit\n  saturating-counter behavior. This removes cold backward-loop redirects\n  without enlarging the target structure or putting a return-stack lookup on\n  the fetch critical path; trained branches retain dynamic behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add per-entry valid state, initialize entries invalid, select BTFNT from the B-immediate sign for untrained legal branches, and set validity on resolved branch training.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed cold backward-branch, cold forward-branch, first-training, saturation, and alias-retraining tests to verify prediction recovery and architectural retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
