{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -ryaml -e 'p=YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]); abort \\\"bad id\\\" unless p[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r3s1\\\"; abort \\\"bad category\\\" unless p[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"structural\\\"; e=p[\\\"expected_impact\\\"]; abort \\\"bad impact\\\" unless e.is_a?(Hash) && e[\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\"].is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(e[\\\"confidence\\\"]); abort \\\"bad changes\\\" unless p[\\\"changes\\\"].is_a?(Array) && p[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.sv|test/test_[\"'^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"hypothesis YAML shape OK\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r3s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r3s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"hypothesis YAML shape OK\nid: hyp-20260711-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Decode-stage branch resolution\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The compact BHT has removed the repeated recovery cost of correctly\n  predicted loop branches, but direction changes and predictor alias/cold\n  misses still redirect only after the instruction reaches EX. Each of those\n  events currently discards two younger fetch/decode slots. The prior return\n  predictor showed that adding more lookup logic to fetch harms Fmax, so the\n  remaining recovery latency should be reduced behind the fetch boundary.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve conditional branch direction and target in ID using a dedicated\n  decode bypass network from the preceding EX result, MEM result, and normal\n  writeback path. An ID-detected mismatch redirects fetch immediately while\n  retaining the branch in ID/EX; a carried early-resolved bit prevents EX from\n  issuing a duplicate redirect. Load-dependent branches retain a precise\n  interlock until their value is available. This turns direction-mispredict\n  recovery from two discarded younger slots into one without extending the\n  predictor's fetch-critical lookup cone or changing retirement width.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add ID/EX metadata recording a branch already resolved in decode so execute can preserve the resolved PC without a second recovery.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add validated conditional-branch compare/target logic plus EX, MEM, and writeback operand bypass selection, and emit an early misprediction redirect only when source data is ready.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Retain normal branch execution, training, RVFI pc_wdata, and trap behavior while suppressing duplicate redirects for ID-resolved branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Distinguish an ID redirect from an EX redirect: flush only the fetched wrong-path slot for the former, preserve the resolving branch, and interlock load-dependent decode branches until forwardable.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire decode-stage forward sources and early redirect into fetch and hazard control while keeping the existing EX recovery path for JALR and unresolved cases.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed tests for independent and ALU-dependent branch recovery in ID, load-dependent branch interlock, predictor mismatch flushing, RVFI order, and exact pc_wdata sequencing.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
