{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r4s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Two-entry instruction skid queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The CoreMark cosim injects roughly 22% instruction-bus backpressure, and\n  the current front end turns every unready imem cycle into a full fetch and\n  decode bubble. The successful branch work has already reduced redirect\n  waste, so absorbing independent delivery stalls is now a larger structural\n  source of lost issue slots.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational IF-to-ID payload with a two-entry, PC-tagged\n  instruction skid queue. Fetch fills an empty queue slot whenever imem is\n  ready while ID independently consumes the head, allowing a previously\n  fetched instruction to enter decode during a later imem stall. Each entry\n  carries its predictor-selected successor so sequential prefetch remains\n  correct; EX and ID redirects synchronously invalidate younger queued\n  entries and restart fetch at the resolved target. This keeps the existing\n  single-retire pipeline and RVFI boundary intact while converting many\n  isolated zero-wait misses into no-bubble cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
