{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; h=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r5s1.yaml\\\"); abort(\\\"bad id\\\") unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r5s1\\\"; abort(\\\"bad category\\\") unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"structural\\\"; abort(\\\"bad change path\\\") unless h[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts JSON.generate(h)'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260711-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"One-entry decoupled store buffer\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"motivation\":\"Random dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage whenever a\\nstore reaches EX/MEM, even though a completed store has no register result\\nand most following CoreMark instructions are independent. The failed fetch\\nqueue showed that broad front-end buffering costs too much Fmax, so the\\nnext decoupling point should be off the critical fetch and execute paths.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Insert a one-entry write buffer between MEM and the dmem pins. A store may\\nretire into an empty buffer in one cycle even when dmemReady is low; the\\nbuffer holds its aligned address, replicated data, and byte enables until\\nthe bus accepts it. Loads and a second store wait until the older buffered\\nstore drains, preserving in-order memory visibility, while independent\\nALU/control instructions continue through the existing single-retire\\npipeline. This converts isolated store-side bus stalls into useful work\\nwithout lengthening the predictor lookup or EX arithmetic cone.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/store_buffer.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a one-entry valid/ready write buffer that captures an aligned store transaction, drives dmem until accepted, and exposes empty/drain state.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Route stores through the buffer, permit an empty-buffer store to advance without dmemReady, and retain exact RVFI store address, mask, and data fields at retirement.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace unconditional store-side dmem freezes with buffer-full and ordered-load interlocks while retaining the existing load and redirect priorities.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire store enqueue, buffer drain, dmem pins, and memory-order status through the existing MEM and hazard controls.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Add randomized dmem-stall cases proving independent instructions advance behind a buffered store, younger loads and stores wait for drain, and RVFI/order/memory data remain exact.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
