\": {\"motivation\": \"Direct branches and JALs already avoid most front-end recovery, but canonical\\nfunction returns still default to the sequential path until EX. CoreMark's\\nsmall helper routines make this a recurring remaining control-flow penalty.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Recognize only canonical returns (JALR x0, x1, 0) in decode and use the\\nexisting EX/MEM/WB bypass network to form the aligned x1 target there. When\\nx1 is ready, redirect fetch one cycle earlier and mark the control transfer\\nresolved so EX preserves its normal RVFI pc_wdata without issuing a duplicate\\nredirect. This is a return-specific late predictor: unlike the prior RAS, it\\nadds no state, tag, or target mux to the fetch-critical BHT lookup cone; unlike\\nthe broad JALR experiment, it leaves calls and arbitrary indirect jumps on the\\nproven EX path. Load-dependent or misaligned returns retain EX resolution and\\nexact trap behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker to denote a control transfer resolved in decode, without carrying a successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect legal canonical returns, reuse the established operand bypass/readiness checks to calculate the masked aligned target, and emit a decode redirect only for a capturable non-faulting return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the generalized decode-resolution marker for canonical returns while retaining the existing JALR link, target, and misalignment-trap calculations for retirement correctness.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decode return-recovery request through the existing older-EX redirect priority and fetch-control interfaces without changing branch_predictor lookup logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add canonical-return cases for register-file, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned targets; check one-cycle recovery, RVFI PC/order, and that noncanonical JALRs still use EX recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker to denote a control transfer resolved in decode, without carrying a successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect legal canonical returns, reuse the established operand bypass/readiness checks to calculate the masked aligned target, and emit a decode redirect only for a capturable non-faulting return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the generalized decode-resolution marker for canonical returns while retaining the existing JALR link, target, and misalignment-trap calculations for retirement correctness.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decode return-recovery request through the existing older-EX redirect priority and fetch-control interfaces without changing branch_predictor lookup logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add canonical-return cases for register-file, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned targets; check one-cycle recovery, RVFI PC/order, and that noncanonical JALRs still use EX recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 319.82, \"delta_pct\": -8.26, \"vs_baseline\": 13.08, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.28, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4136096, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8025, \"ff\": 1926, \"seeds\": [132.28, 131.84, 155.88], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:10:21.056667Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -8.26%): Decode-resolving canonical JALR returns with bypass readiness, load-dependency, and alignment 