{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\"),(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis)] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r '[.id,.title,.category,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\tIterative divide execution unit\tbroken\t\t\tReplace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r2s1\tBounded radix-4 divide pipeline\tbroken\t\t\tReplace only the real divide/remainder ALU path with an eight-cycle radix-4\\niterative unit. A precise EX interlock will accept each divide exactly once,\\nallow older MEM/WB work to drain, retain the DIV payload while busy, and\\nadvance one normal EX/MEM result on the fixed completion cycle. Eight cycles\\nkeeps total fetch-to-retire latency within the existing 20-step formal depth,\\nwhile removing the large combinational divider from the ordinary EX critical\\npath. MUL remains combinational and the ALTOPS behavior remains equivalent\\nfor formal checks.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r3s1\tDecode-stage branch resolution\timprovement\t344.27\t8.89\tResolve conditional branch direction and target in ID using a dedicated\\ndecode bypass network from the preceding EX result, MEM result, and normal\\nwriteback path. An ID-detected mismatch redirects fetch immediately while\\nretaining the branch in ID/EX; a carried early-resolved bit prevents EX from\\nissuing a duplicate redirect. Load-dependent branches retain a precise\\ninterlock until their value is available. This turns direction-mispredict\\nrecovery from two discarded younger slots into one without extending the\\npredictor's fetch-critical lookup cone or changing retirement width.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r4s1\tTwo-entry instruction skid queue\tregression\t334.25\t-2.91\tReplace the combinational IF-to-ID payload with a two-entry, PC-tagged\\ninstruction skid queue. Fetch fills an empty queue slot whenever imem is\\nready while ID independently consumes the head, allowing a previously\\nfetched instruction to enter decode during a later imem stall. Each entry\\ncarries its predictor-selected successor so sequential prefetch remains\\ncorrect; EX and ID redirects synchronously invalidate younger queued\\nentries and restart fetch at the resolved target. This keeps the existing\\nsingle-retire pipeline and RVFI boundary intact while converting many\\nisolated zero-wait misses into no-bubble cycles.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r5s1\tOne-entry decoupled store buffer\tplacement_failed\t\t\tInsert a one-entry write buffer between MEM and the dmem pins. A store may\\nretire into an empty buffer in one cycle even when dmemReady is low; the\\nbuffer holds its aligned address, replicated data, and byte enables until\\nthe bus accepts it. Loads and a second store wait until the older buffered\\nstore drains, preserving in-order memory visibility, while independent\\nALU/control instructions continue through the existing single-retire\\npipeline. This converts isolated store-side bus stalls into useful work\\nwithout lengthening the predictor lookup or EX arithmetic cone.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r6s1\tDecode-stage JALR recovery\tbroken\t\t\tExtend the existing decode-stage control-resolution path to legal JALR\\ninstructions. Reuse its EX/MEM/WB operand bypasses to calculate the masked\\nrs1+immediate target in ID and redirect one cycle before EX whenever the\\nsource is ready and the target is aligned. Carry a single generalized\\ncontrol-resolved bit into EX to suppress duplicate recovery; load-dependent\\nor misaligned JALRs retain the current EX path so their interlock and trap\\nsemantics stay exact. This changes recovery-stage topology without adding a\\ntarget lookup or return stack to the fetch-critical predictor cone.\\n\nhyp-20260711-002-r7s1\tForwarded decode-stage JALR recovery\tbroken\t\t\tResolve legal, aligned JALR targets in ID using the existing EX/MEM/WB\\nbypass priority, then redirect fetch one stage earlier. Crucially, latch\\nthose same selected source operands into ID/EX so EX, register writeback,\\nand RVFI rs1_rdata retain the architecturally current value; the previous\\ndecode-JALR attempt redirected using a forwarded value while retaining a\\nstale operand, which broke the formal register check. Load-dependent and\\nmisaligned JALRs remain on the precise EX path, and a resolved-in-ID flag\\nsuppresses only the duplicate EX redirect.\\n\nbaseline-bench-7155d3c\tBaseline retest for cores/bench\tmicro_opt\timprovement\t282.82\t0.0\nhyp-20260711-001-r1s0\tPrune dead EX branch payload\tmicro_opt\tregression\t302.55\t6.98\nhyp-20260711-002-r1s1\tIterative divide execution unit\tstructural\tbroken\t\t\nhyp-20260711-003-r1s2\tCompact direct branch predictor\tpredictor\timprovement\t316.16\t11.79\nhyp-20260711-001-r2s0\tDecode-aware load-use interlock\tmicro_opt\tbroken\t\t\nhyp-20260711-002-r2s1\tBounded radix-4 divide pipeline\tstructural\tbroken\t\t\nhyp-20260711-003-r2s2\tCommitted return-stack JALR predictor\tpredictor\tregression\t308.55\t-2.41\nhyp-20260711-001-r3s0\tStatic backward branch fast path\tmicro_opt\tregression\t316.17\t0.0\nhyp-20260711-002-r3s1\tDecode-stage branch resolution\tstructural\timprovement\t344.27\t8.89\nhyp-20260711-003-r3s2\tCold-start BTFNT branch fallback\tpredictor\tregression\t308.36\t-2.47\nhyp-20260711-001-r4s0\tSingle narrow RV32M multiplier\tmicro_opt\tregression\t321.75\t-6.54\nhyp-