": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add per-entry valid state, initialize entries invalid, select BTFNT from the B-immediate sign for untrained legal branches, and set validity on resolved branch training.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cold backward-branch, cold forward-branch, first-training, saturation, and alias-retraining tests to verify prediction recovery and architectural retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add per-entry valid state, initialize entries invalid, select BTFNT from the B-immediate sign for untrained legal branches, and set validity on resolved branch training.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cold backward-branch, cold forward-branch, first-training, saturation, and alias-retraining tests to verify prediction recovery and architectural retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.36, \"delta_pct\": -2.47, \"vs_baseline\": 9.03, \"fmax_mhz\": 130.11, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4219411, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10120, \"ff\": 1952, \"seeds\": [125.17, 130.11, 132.28], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:40:22.900337Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r3s2 (regression, -2.47%): On this CoreMark front end, adding a per-entry valid-bit read and BTFNT direction mux to the BHT lookup cone costs more than it saves on first-iteration backward-loop redirects, so cold-start policy must not lengthen the fetch-critical predictor path without a larger benefit.\"}\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Two-entry instruction skid queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The CoreMark cosim injects roughly 22% instruction-bus backpressure, and\\nthe current front end turns every unready imem cycle into a full fetch and\\ndecode bubble. The successful branch work has already reduced redirect\\nwaste, so absorbing independent delivery stalls is now a larger structural\\nsource of lost issue slots.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The CoreMark cosim injects roughly 22% instruction-bus backpressure, and\\nthe current front end turns every unready imem cycle into a full fetch and\\ndecode bubble. The successful branch work has already reduced redirect\\nwaste, so absorbing independent delivery stalls is now a larger structural\\nsource of lost issue slots.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational IF-to-ID payload with a two-entry, PC-tagged\\ninstruction skid queue. Fetch fills an empty queue slot whenever imem is\\nready while ID independently consumes the head, allowing a previously\\nfetched instruction to enter decode during a later imem stall. Each entry\\ncarries its predictor-selected successor so sequential prefetch remains\\ncorrect; EX and ID redirects synchronously invalidate younger queued\\nentries and restart fetch at the resolved target. This keeps the existing\\nsingle-retire pipeline and RVFI boundary intact while converting many\\nisolated zero-wait misses into no-bubble cycles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 334.25, \"delta_pct\": -2.91, \"vs_baseline\": 18.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.65, \"ipc_