etto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r6s1/formal/last_run-23485.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r6s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-23485/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Taken-biased BHT cold start\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current BHT initializes every counter as weakly not taken, so each\\nnewly encountered counted-loop back edge pays a recovery before the table\\nlearns its overwhelmingly taken steady-state direction. CoreMark repeatedly\\nenters compact loops, while the prior BTFNT fallback showed that adding\\nlookup logic to address this warm-up cost hurts Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current BHT initializes every counter as weakly not taken, so each\\nnewly encountered counted-loop back edge pays a recovery before the table\\nlearns its overwhelmingly taken steady-state direction. CoreMark repeatedly\\nenters compact loops, while the prior BTFNT fallback showed that adding\\nlookup logic to address this warm-up cost hurts Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Initialize the existing sixteen two-bit BHT counters to weakly taken\\n(2'b10) instead of weakly not taken (2'b01). This removes the first-taken\\nmisprediction for cold loop back edges with no new state, muxing, PC hash,\\nor fetch-path logic. A first not-taken forward branch still trains the same\\ncounter to weakly not taken after one recovery, retaining normal dynamic\\nbehavior and existing decode-stage training semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Change BHT reset initialization to weakly taken while retaining the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Change BHT reset initialization to weakly taken while retaining the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 338.8, \"delta_pct\": -1.9, \"vs_baseline\": 19.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.55, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10700, \"ff\": 1927, \"seeds\": [137.44, 142.25, 140.55], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T16:45:01.518248Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.90%): With a two-bit BHT already in the fetch path, weakly-taken reset harms CoreMark more through cold forward/not-taken branches and aliases than it saves on first counted-loop back edges, so the weakly-not-taken cold bias is the better default.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
