d address, replicated data, and byte enables until\\nthe bus accepts it. Loads and a second store wait until the older buffered\\nstore drains, preserving in-order memory visibility, while independent\\nALU/control instructions continue through the existing single-retire\\npipeline. This converts isolated store-side bus stalls into useful work\\nwithout lengthening the predictor lookup or EX arithmetic cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/store_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry valid/ready write buffer that captures an aligned store transaction, drives dmem until accepted, and exposes empty/drain state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route stores through the buffer, permit an empty-buffer store to advance without dmemReady, and retain exact RVFI store address, mask, and data fields at retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace unconditional store-side dmem freezes with buffer-full and ordered-load interlocks while retaining the existing load and redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire store enqueue, buffer drain, dmem pins, and memory-order status through the existing MEM and hazard controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized dmem-stall cases proving independent instructions advance behind a buffered store, younger loads and stores wait for drain, and RVFI/order/memory data remain exact.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/store_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry valid/ready write buffer that captures an aligned store transaction, drives dmem until accepted, and exposes empty/drain state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route stores through the buffer, permit an empty-buffer store to advance without dmemReady, and retain 