th until EX. CoreMark's\\\\\\\\nsmall helper routines make this a recurring remaining control-flow penalty.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Direct branches and JALs already avoid most front-end recovery, but canonical\\\\\\\\nfunction returns still default to the sequential path until EX. CoreMark's\\\\\\\\nsmall helper routines make this a recurring remaining control-flow penalty.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recognize only canonical returns (JALR x0, x1, 0) in decode and use the\\\\\\\\nexisting EX/MEM/WB bypass network to form the aligned x1 target there. When\\\\\\\\nx1 is ready, redirect fetch one cycle earlier and mark the control transfer\\\\\\\\nresolved so EX preserves its normal RVFI pc_wdata without issuing a duplicate\\\\\\\\nredirect. This is a return-specific late predictor: unlike the prior RAS, it\\\\\\\\nadds no state, tag, or target mux to the fetch-critical BHT lookup cone; unlike\\\\\\\\nthe broad JALR experiment, it leaves calls and arbitrary indirect jumps on the\\\\\\\\nproven EX path. Load-dependent or misaligned returns retain EX resolution and\\\\\\\\nexact trap behavior.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 3, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker to denote a control transfer resolved in decode, without carrying a successor payload.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Detect legal canonical returns, reuse the established operand bypass/readiness checks to calculate the masked aligned target, and emit a decode redirect only for a capturable non-faulting return.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Honor the generalized decode-resolution marker for canonical returns while retaining the existing JALR link, target, and misalignment-trap calculations for retirement correctness.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Wire the decode return-recovery request through the existing older-EX redirect priority and fetch-control interfaces without changing branch_predictor lookup logic.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add canonical-return cases for register-file, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned targets; check one-cycle recovery, RVFI PC/order, and that noncanonical JALRs still use EX recovery.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 3, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker to denote a control transfer resolved in decode, without carrying a successor payload.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Detect legal canonical returns, reuse the established operand bypass/readiness checks to calculate the masked aligned target, and emit a decode redirect only for a capturable non-faulting return.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Honor the generalized decode-resolution marker for canonical returns while retaining the existing JALR link, target, and misalignment-trap calculations for retirement correctness.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Wire the decode return-recovery request through the existing older-EX redirect priority and fetch-control interfaces without changing branch_predictor lookup logic.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add canonical-return cases for register-file, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned targets; check one-cycle recovery, RVFI PC/order, and that noncanonical JALRs still use EX recovery.\\\\\\\"}], \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"regression\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness\\\\\\\": 319.82, \\\\\\\"delta_pct\\\\\\\": -8.26, \\\\\\\"vs_baseline\\\\\\\": 13.08, \\\\\\\"fmax_mhz\\\\\\\": 132.28, \\\\\\\"ipc_coremark\\\\\\\": 2e-06, \\\\\\\"cycles\\\\\\\": 4136096, \\\\\\\"iterations\\\\\\\": 10, \\\\\\\"lut4\\\\\\\": 8025, \\\\\\\"ff\\\\\\\": 1926, \\\\\\\"seeds\\\\\\\": [132.28, 131.84, 155.88], \\\\\\\"formal_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"cosim_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"implementation_notes\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-07-11T17:10:21.056667Z\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"slot\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"round_id\\\\\\\": 7, \\\\\\\"lesson\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -8.26%): Decode-resolving canonical JALR returns with bypass readiness, load-dependency, and alignment checks regresses CoreMark when the saved recovery slot on short helper returns cannot amortize the added ID-stage control/target logic, so return recovery needs a lower-cost path or stronger dynamic evidence.\\\\\\\"}\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): An iterative EX divider must preserve the pipeline's valid/retirement progress contract while it holds ID/EX; freezing around a multicycle response can make DIV/REM formal assumptions unreachable and fail liveness even when unrelated instructions pass.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (improvement, +11.79%): A compact PC-indexed two-bit BHT that predicts direct B-immediate targets and JALs removes the repeated two-slot EX recovery bubbles in CoreMark's short counted loops, provided EX compares resolved and carried predicted next PCs before flushing.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r2s2 (regression, -2.41%): For this CoreMark front end, a committed four-entry RAS's canonical-JALR decode, stack-top target mux, and EX training state cost more than eliminating return recovery bubbles, so return prediction must stay off the fetch-critical path unless its dynamic benefit is demonstrably larger.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r3s1 (improvement, +8.89%): Resolving conditional branches in ID with EX/MEM/WB operand bypasses and a load-use interlock recovers one CoreMark mispredict slot without extending the fetch predictor's Fmax-critical lookup cone, provided the carried early-resolved bit suppresses EX's duplicate redirect.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r3s2 (regression, -2.47%): On this CoreMark front end, adding a per-entry valid-bit read and BTFNT direction mux to the BHT lookup cone costs more than it saves on first-iteration backward-loop redirects, so cold-start policy must not lengthen the fetch-critical predictor path without a larger benefit.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r5s0 (regression, -23.69%): Once branches are already resolved in ID, carrying a 32-bit successor plus direction and misalignment state through ID/EX only trades EX recomputation for wider registered routing without reducing CoreMark recovery bubbles, so duplicate control logic should remain unless post-route timing proves the payload is cheaper.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r5s2 (improvement, +0.31%): When a legal conditional branch is operand-ready in ID, training its two-bit BHT under the same capture/redirect gate removes a cycle of stale counter state for nearby loop branches and aliases without lengthening the fetch lookup cone.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r6s0 (improvement, +0.95%): Sharing a single unsigned magnitude quotient/remainder cone across DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU modestly reduces divider LUT/routing pressure while preserving RV32M sign, zero-divisor, and INT_MIN/-1 behavior through explicit result restoration.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.90%): With a two-bit BHT already in the fetch path, weakly-taken reset harms CoreMark more through cold forward/not-taken branches and aliases than it saves on first counted-loop back edges, so the weakly-not-taken cold bias is the better default.\\\\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -8.26%): Decode-resolving canonical JALR returns with bypass readiness, load-dependency, and alignment checks regresses CoreMark when the saved recovery slot on short helper returns cannot amortize the added ID-stage control/target logic, so return recovery needs a lower-cost path or stronger dynamic evidence.\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"$schema\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\"],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":       {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"pattern\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\\\\\\\"},\\\\n    \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":    {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"minLength\\\\\\\": 5},\\\\n    \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"enum\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"extension\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"memory\\\\\\\"]},\\\\n    \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\":  {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"minLength\\\\\\\": 20},\\\\n    \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\":  {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"minLength\\\\\\\": 20},\\\\n    \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\"],\\\\n      \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"integer\\\\\\\"},\\\\n        \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"enum\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"low\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"high\\\\\\\"]}\\\\n      }\\\\n    },\\\\n    \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"array\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"minItems\\\\\\\": 1,\\\\n      \\\\\\\"items\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"object\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"required\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\"],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"properties\\\\\\\": {\\\\n          \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\":        {\\\\n            \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\",\\\\n            \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\\\\\\\",\\\\n            \\\\\\\"pattern\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.py)$\\\\\\\"\\\\n          },\\\\n          \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"string\\\\\\\"}\\\\n        }\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.fmax_mhz // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.lut4 // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.cycles // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), .hypothesis.hypothesis] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | column -t -s \\\\\\\"'$'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t' && rg -n -C 2 'hyp-20260711-003-r[1-7]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && find cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort | tail -20\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.fmax_mhz // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.lut4 // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), (.cycles // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), .hypothesis.hypothesis] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | column -t -s \\\\\\\"'$'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t' && rg -n -C 2 'hyp-20260711-003-r[1-7]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && find cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort | tail -20\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2  Compact direct branch predictor        improvement  316.16  11.79  133.4   10561  4219411  Add a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\\\\\\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\\\\\\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\\\\\\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\\\\\\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\\\\\\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\\\\\\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r2s2  Committed return-stack JALR predictor  regression   308.55  -2.41  129.72  10293  4204229  Extend the existing direct predictor with a tiny committed return-address\\\\\\\\nstack. Detect canonical RV32 calls and returns in fetch: predict a JALR\\\\\\\\nreturn through the stack top, while EX pushes PC+4 for resolved calls and\\\\\\\\npops only resolved canonical returns. Keeping updates at resolution avoids\\\\\\\\ncorrupting predictor state on a mispredicted speculative path, and avoids\\\\\\\\nthe tags, target RAM, and lookup delay of a general indirect BTB.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r3s2  Cold-start BTFNT branch fallback       regression   308.36  -2.47  130.11  10120  4219411  Add one validity bit per existing BHT entry and use static backward-taken,\\\\\\\\nforward-not-taken prediction only while that entry is untrained. On the\\\\\\\\nfirst resolved branch, mark the entry valid and retain the present two-bit\\\\\\\\nsaturating-counter behavior. This removes cold backward-loop redirects\\\\\\\\nwithout enlarging the target structure or putting a return-stack lookup on\\\\\\\\nthe fetch critical path; trained branches retain dynamic behavior.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r4s2  Folded-PC BHT indexing                 regression   317.51  -7.77  131.72  10793  4148503  Replace the direct BHT index with a four-bit folded-PC hash, for example\\\\\\\\nPC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], for both lookup and resolved-branch training. This\\\\\\\\nretains the existing 16 counters, reset policy, direct B-immediate target\\\\\\\\npath, and JAL behavior, but distributes otherwise congruent branch PCs\\\\\\\\nacross the table. Four local XOR gates should be materially cheaper than\\\\\\\\nanother predictor state array or target lookup, while fewer alias-driven\\\\\\\\ndirection misses improve CoreMark IPC.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r5s2  Decode-stage BHT training              improvement  345.35  0.31   143.27  10700  4148503  Train the existing two-bit BHT directly from the validated, operand-ready\\\\\\\\ndecode-stage branch result and remove the redundant EX-to-predictor training\\\\\\\\npath. This advances counter updates by one cycle without changing BHT size,\\\\\\\\nindexing, reset policy, direct-target generation, or the fetch lookup cone.\\\\\\\\nIt should reduce short-loop and closely spaced alias recovery bubbles while\\\\\\\\npreserving the successful ID-stage redirect and EX fallback behavior.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r6s2  Taken-biased BHT cold start            regression   338.8   -1.9   140.55  10700  4148503  Initialize the existing sixteen two-bit BHT counters to weakly taken\\\\\\\\n(2'b10) instead of weakly not taken (2'b01). This removes the first-taken\\\\\\\\nmisprediction for cold loop back edges with no new state, muxing, PC hash,\\\\\\\\nor fetch-path logic. A first not-taken forward branch still trains the same\\\\\\\\ncounter to weakly not taken after one recovery, retaining normal dynamic\\\\\\\\nbehavior and existing decode-stage training semantics.\\\\\\\\n\\\\nhyp-20260711-003-r7s2  Decode-assisted return recovery        regression   319.82  -8.26  132.28  8025   4136096  Recognize only canonical returns (JALR x0, x1, 0) in decode and use the\\\\\\\\nexisting EX/MEM/WB bypass network to form the aligned x1 target there. When\\\\\\\\nx1 is ready, redirect fetch one cycle earlier and mark the control transfer\\\\\\\\nresolved so EX preserves its normal RVFI pc_wdata without issuing a duplicate\\\\\\\\nredirect. This is a return-specific late predictor: unlike the prior RAS, it\\\\\\\\nadds no state, tag, or target mux to the fetch-critical BHT lookup cone; unlike\\\\\\\\nthe broad JALR experiment, it leaves calls and arbitrary indirect jumps on the\\\\\\\\nproven EX path. Load-dependent or misaligned returns retain EX resolution and\\\\\\\\nexact trap behavior.\\\\\\\\n\\\\n2-{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Prune dead EX branch payload\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\\\\\\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\\\\\\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\\\\\\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\\\\\\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and\\\\\\\\ntheir EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on\\\\\\\\nduplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint\\\\\\\\nwhile preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller\\\\\\\\nEX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 5, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 5, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\\\\\\\"}], \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"regression\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness\\\\\\\": 302.55, \\\\\\\"delta_pct\\\\\\\": 6.98, \\\\\\\"vs_baseline\\\\\\\": 6.98, \\\\\\\"fmax_mhz\\\\\\\": 135.89, \\\\\\\"ipc_coremark\\\\\\\": 2e-06, \\\\\\\"cycles\\\\\\\": 4491485, \\\\\\\"iterations\\\\\\\": 10, \\\\\\\"lut4\\\\\\\": 10363, \\\\\\\"ff\\\\\\\": 1865, \\\\\\\"seeds\\\\\\\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \\\\\\\"formal_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"cosim_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"implementation_notes\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"slot\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"round_id\\\\\\\": 1}\\\\n3-{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Iterative divide execution unit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\\\\\\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\\\\\\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\\\\\\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\\\\\\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\\\\\\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\\\\\\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\\\\\\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\\\\\\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\\\\\\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\\\\\\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\\\\\\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\\\\\\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\\\\\\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 8, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_alu.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\\\\\\\"}]}, \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 8, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"test/test_alu.py\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage 