ost a\\\\\\\\nmeaningful remaining front-end loss.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Resolve legal, aligned JALR targets in ID using the existing EX/MEM/WB\\\\\\\\nbypass priority, then redirect fetch one stage earlier. Crucially, latch\\\\\\\\nthose same selected source operands into ID/EX so EX, register writeback,\\\\\\\\nand RVFI rs1_rdata retain the architecturally current value; the previous\\\\\\\\ndecode-JALR attempt redirected using a forwarded value while retaining a\\\\\\\\nstale operand, which broke the formal register check. Load-dependent and\\\\\\\\nmisaligned JALRs remain on the precise EX path, and a resolved-in-ID flag\\\\\\\\nsuppresses only the duplicate EX redirect.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"expected_impact\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\\\\\": 4, \\\\\\\"confidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"changes\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Generalize the ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID marker while retaining the existing compact payload.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Apply the established EX/MEM/WB bypass priority to legal JALR target calculation and latch the selected operands, not raw regfile values, into ID/EX for JALR.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Use the control-resolved-in-ID marker to suppress only duplicate JALR recovery while preserving link writeback, misalignment trapping, and RVFI operand reporting.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/core.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Route the validated decode-stage JALR redirect through the existing redirect-priority path without adding predictor lookup logic.\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Preserve load-use and dmem-stall