{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"predictor\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"), (.hypothesis.hypothesis // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\tCompact direct branch predictor\timprovement\t316.16\t11.79\tAdd a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r2s2\tCommitted return-stack JALR predictor\tregression\t308.55\t-2.41\tExtend the existing direct predictor with a tiny committed return-address\\nstack. Detect canonical RV32 calls and returns in fetch: predict a JALR\\nreturn through the stack top, while EX pushes PC+4 for resolved calls and\\npops only resolved canonical returns. Keeping updates at resolution avoids\\ncorrupting predictor state on a mispredicted speculative path, and avoids\\nthe tags, target RAM, and lookup delay of a general indirect BTB.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r3s2\tCold-start BTFNT branch fallback\tregression\t308.36\t-2.47\tAdd one validity bit per existing BHT entry and use static backward-taken,\\nforward-not-taken prediction only while that entry is untrained. On the\\nfirst resolved branch, mark the entry valid and retain the present two-bit\\nsaturating-counter behavior. This removes cold backward-loop redirects\\nwithout enlarging the target structure or putting a return-stack lookup on\\nthe fetch critical path; trained branches retain dynamic behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r4s2\tFolded-PC BHT indexing\tregression\t317.51\t-7.77\tReplace the direct BHT index with a four-bit folded-PC hash, for example\\nPC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], for both lookup and resolved-branch training. This\\nretains the existing 16 counters, reset policy, direct B-immediate target\\npath, and JAL behavior, but distributes otherwise congruent branch PCs\\nacross the table. Four local XOR gates should be materially cheaper than\\nanother predictor state array or target lookup, while fewer alias-driven\\ndirection misses improve CoreMark IPC.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r5s2\tDecode-stage BHT training\timprovement\t345.35\t0.31\tTrain the existing two-bit BHT directly from the validated, operand-ready\\ndecode-stage branch result and remove the redundant EX-to-predictor training\\npath. This advances counter updates by one cycle without changing BHT size,\\nindexing, reset policy, direct-target generation, or the fetch lookup cone.\\nIt should reduce short-loop and closely spaced alias recovery bubbles while\\npreserving the successful ID-stage redirect and EX fallback behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r6s2\tTaken-biased BHT cold start\tregression\t338.8\t-1.9\tInitialize the existing sixteen two-bit BHT counters to weakly taken\\n(2'b10) instead of weakly not taken (2'b01). This removes the first-taken\\nmisprediction for cold loop back edges with no new state, muxing, PC hash,\\nor fetch-path logic. A first not-taken forward branch still trains the same\\ncounter to weakly not taken after one recovery, retaining normal dynamic\\nbehavior and existing decode-stage training semantics.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r7s2\tDecode-assisted return recovery\tregression\t319.82\t-8.26\tRecognize only canonical returns (JALR x0, x1, 0) in decode and use the\\nexisting EX/MEM/WB bypass network to form the aligned x1 target there. When\\nx1 is ready, redirect fetch one cycle earlier and mark the control transfer\\nresolved so EX preserves its normal RVFI pc_wdata without issuing a duplicate\\nredirect. This is a return-specific late predictor: unlike the prior RAS, it\\nadds no state, tag, or target mux to the fetch-critical BHT lookup cone; unlike\\nthe broad JALR experiment, it leaves calls and arbitrary indirect jumps on the\\nproven EX path. Load-dependent or misaligned returns retain EX resolution and\\nexact trap behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r8s2\tJAL-only fetch predictor\timprovement\t353.6\t1.43\tReplace the conditional two-bit BHT prediction with a minimal direct-JAL\\nfetch predictor: JAL is still sent immediately to its encoded target, but\\nconditional branches always fetch PC+4 and rely on the established\\noperand-ready ID redirect for taken outcomes. Remove BHT state and its\\ndecode-stage training interface. This trades the limited remaining benefit\\nof speculative conditional direction (principally load-dependent branches)\\nfor a shorter, lower-fanout fetch-to-PC path while retaining bubble-free\\ndirect calls and jumps.\\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
