 legal.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-stage branch training to the existing predictor and remove the superseded EX-stage training connections while retaining all redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove redundant BHT training outputs; keep branch execution, misalignment traps, resolved pc_next, and EX recovery for branches not resolved in ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the earlier committed decode-stage training event without altering the sixteen-entry counter lookup, direct JAL prediction, or fetch-critical prediction selection.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed back-to-back and aliasing branch cases proving that ID-stage training is visible at the next lookup, saturates correctly, and preserves redirect and RVFI PC ordering.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 345.35, \"delta_pct\": 0.31, \"vs_baseline\": 22.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 143.27, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10700, \"ff\": 1927, \"seeds\": [143.27, 132.68, 143.58], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:33:09.477998Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r5s2 (improvement, +0.31%): When a legal conditional branch is operand-ready in ID, training its two-bit BHT under the same capture/redirect gate removes a cycle of stale counter state for nearby loop branches and aliases without lengthening the fetch lookup cone.\"}\n17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Shared magnitude divide datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\\nremainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\\nselectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\\neven though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\\nremainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\\nselectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\\neven though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with a shared magnitude\\nquotient/remainder datapath: derive operand magnitudes only for signed\\noperations, perform one unsigned divide and modulo pair, and restore the\\nquotient or remainder sign according to RV32M rules. Keep explicit\\ndivide-by-zero behavior and retain the magnitude-based INT_MIN/-1 results.\\nThis halves the divider-class operator count without changing latency,\\nforwarding, retirement, or the fetch-critical predictor path, so it should\\nimprove Tang Nano placement and Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU vectors across signedness boundaries, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and randomized values to validate the shared datapath.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and 