xecution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, ((.delta_pct // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring), ((.fitness // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring)] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\") | \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nID: \\\\\\\\(.id)\\\\\\\\nTITLE: \\\\\\\\(.title)\\\\\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\\\\\(.outcome) delta=\\\\\\\\((.delta_pct // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring)\\\\\\\\nHYPOTHESIS: \\\\\\\\((.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\") | gsub(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"; \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, ((.delta_pct // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring), ((.fitness // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring)] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.category == \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\") | \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nID: \\\\\\\\(.id)\\\\\\\\nTITLE: \\\\\\\\(.title)\\\\\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\\\\\(.outcome) delta=\\\\\\\\((.delta_pct // \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\") | tostring)\\\\\\\\nHYPOTHESIS: \\\\\\\\((.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\") | gsub(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"; \\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"baseline-bench-7155d3c\\tBaseline retest for cores/bench\\timprovement\\t0.0\\t282.82\\nhyp-20260711-001-r1s0\\tPrune dead EX branch payload\\tregression\\t6.98\\t302.55\\nhyp-20260711-001-r2s0\\tDecode-aware load-use interlock\\tbroken\\tn/a\\tn/a\\nhyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\tStatic backward branch fast path\\tregression\\t0.0\\t316.17\\nhyp-20260711-001-r4s0\\tSingle narrow RV32M multiplier\\tregression\\t-6.54\\t321.75\\nhyp-20260711-001-r5s0\\tAuthoritative decode branch resolution\\tregression\\t-23.69\\t262.72\\nhyp-20260711-001-r6s0\\tShared magnitude divide datapath\\timprovement\\t0.95\\t348.63\\nhyp-20260711-001-r7s0\\tOpcode-aware load-use interlock\\tbroken\\tn/a\\tn/a\\nhyp-20260711-001-r8s0\\tUnsigned product high-half correction\\tregression\\t-46.02\\t188.19\\nhyp-20260711-001-r9s0\\tSplit RVFI retirement-order counter\\tregression\\t-61.98\\t134.43\\nhyp-20260711-001-r10s0\\tRegister-slice the RVFI retirement bundle\\tregression\\t-58.18\\t147.88\\nhyp-20260711-001-r11s0\\tPrune duplicate decode writeback bypass\\tregression\\t-5.81\\t333.04\\n\\nID: baseline-bench-7155d3c\\nTITLE: Baseline retest for cores/bench\\nOUTCOME: improvement delta=0.0\\nHYPOTHESIS: \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\\nTITLE: Prune dead EX branch payload\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=6.98\\nHYPOTHESIS: Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and their EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on duplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint while preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller EX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\\nTITLE: Decode-aware load-use interlock\\nOUTCOME: broken delta=n/a\\nHYPOTHESIS: Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the load-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads the matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store, JALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in CoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding, memory timing, or retirement semantics. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\nTITLE: Static backward branch fast path\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=0.0\\nHYPOTHESIS: Replace the PC-indexed two-bit counter lookup with a stateless backward-taken/forward-not-taken policy for validated conditional branches, while retaining direct-JAL target prediction and existing EX comparison recovery. A negative B-immediate predicts its direct target; forward branches stay sequential. This removes the BHT flops, index mux, reset fanout, and training cone from fetch, avoids the first-iteration loop miss, and should preserve nearly all CoreMark loop IPC at a higher Fmax. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\\nTITLE: Single narrow RV32M multiplier\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-6.54\\nHYPOTHESIS: Select operand extension from the decoded multiply operation and compute one signed 33-by-33 product, selecting its low half for MUL and bits [63:32] for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. This preserves all RV32M signedness semantics while eliminating two parallel multipliers and avoiding the accidental 64-bit operand expansion. The smaller arithmetic fabric should reduce placement pressure and improve Fmax without adding latency or changing IPC. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\\nTITLE: Authoritative decode branch resolution\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-23.69\\nHYPOTHESIS: Make the decode-stage branch decision authoritative for every legal conditional branch once its operands are ready. Carry the resolved taken bit, successor, and target-misalignment fault state through ID/EX so EX selects the recorded result, trains the BHT from the recorded direction, and preserves precise illegal/trap behavior without recomputing a branch comparator or PC-plus-immediate adder. This should shorten the EX control path while retaining the existing load interlock and recovery semantics. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\\nTITLE: Shared magnitude divide datapath\\nOUTCOME: improvement delta=0.95\\nHYPOTHESIS: Replace the four DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with a shared magnitude quotient/remainder datapath: derive operand magnitudes only for signed operations, perform one unsigned divide and modulo pair, and restore the quotient or remainder sign according to RV32M rules. Keep explicit divide-by-zero behavior and retain the magnitude-based INT_MIN/-1 results. This halves the divider-class operator count without changing latency, forwarding, retirement, or the fetch-critical predictor path, so it should improve Tang Nano placement and Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r7s0\\nTITLE: Opcode-aware load-use interlock\\nOUTCOME: broken delta=n/a\\nHYPOTHESIS: Derive conservative rs1/rs2-use qualifiers locally from the fetched opcode in the hazard unit, and gate each load-use comparison with its qualifier. Preserve both-source interlocks for OP, STORE, and BRANCH, rs1 interlocks for OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR, and conservatively treat every other encoding as source-free. This removes false immediate-field alias bubbles without changing decoder control, forwarding, memory ordering, or retirement. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r8s0\\nTITLE: Unsigned product high-half correction\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-46.02\\nHYPOTHESIS: Keep one unsigned 32 by 32 product for MUL and MULHU, then derive MULH and MULHSU high halves from that product with modulo-2^32 sign corrections: subtract b when rs1 is negative and subtract a when rs2 is negative, with only the applicable term used for MULHSU. This removes the two wide signed product cones without changing EX latency, forwarding, retirement, or the proven divide datapath. It should reduce LUT/routing pressure and raise Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\\nTITLE: Split RVFI retirement-order counter\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-61.98\\nHYPOTHESIS: Replace the monolithic 64-bit retirement-order incrementer with a low and high 32-bit counter. Increment the low word on every valid retirement and increment the high word only when the low word wraps; concatenate the words for io_rvfi_order_0. This preserves exact modulo-2^64 strictly increasing RVFI order semantics while shortening the common registered carry chain from 64 to 32 bits, reducing routing pressure without changing IPC. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\\nTITLE: Register-slice the RVFI retirement bundle\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-58.18\\nHYPOTHESIS: Add one dedicated RVFI output register in core.sv. Capture every channel-0 RVFI field and the current order value atomically when MEM/WB retires, then drive the top-level ports solely from that register. The extra fixed observation cycle leaves execution, marker timing, and retirement order unchanged while cutting the MEM/WB/writeback-to-wrapper fanout path. This should improve placed Fmax without extending fetch, ALU, memory, or branch timing cones. \\n\\nID: hyp-20260711-001-r11s0\\nTITLE: Prune duplicate decode writeback bypass\\nOUTCOME: regression delta=-5.81\\nHYPOTHESIS: Remove ID's redundant WB-to-branch operand bypass and its three writeback ports. The regfile already returns wb_w_data for a same-cycle matching read address, making branch_rs1/branch_rs2 identical before the remaining age-prioritized MEM and EX overrides. This eliminates two 5-bit comparators, zero-register tests, and 32-bit mux legs from the early branch-resolution cone, improving Fmax without changing instruction scheduling, IPC, RVFI, or bypass semantics. \\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n -i 'critical|timing|fmax|forward|bypass|load-use|hazard|regfile|fetch' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 24 && rg --files cores/bench/test | sort && sed -n '1,260p' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n -i 'critical|timing|fmax|forward|bypass|load-use|hazard|regfile|fetch' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 24 && rg --files cores/bench/test | sort && sed -n '1,260p' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"11:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Single narrow RV32M multiplier\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The ALU currently builds three unconditional 64-by-64 signed-product\\\\nvariants to serve the four RV32M multiply operations. Those oversized,\\\\nparallel multiplier cones consume substantial LUT and routing resources on\\\\nevery cycle, even though RV32 operands need at most a signed 33-by-33\\\\nproduct to produce every required low or high result bit.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Select operand extension from the decoded multiply operation and compute one\\\\nsigned 33-by-33 product, selecting its low half for MUL and bits [63:32]\\\\nfor MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. This preserves all RV32M signedness semantics\\\\nwhile eliminating two parallel multipliers and avoiding the accidental\\\\n64-bit operand expansion. The smaller arithmetic fabric should reduce\\\\nplacement pressure and improve Fmax without adding latency or changing IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the three unconditional 64-bit product expressions with one operation-selected signed 33-by-33 product; retain the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS mappings and all divide/remainder behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add or retain boundary and randomized vectors for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU, including signed-negative and maximal-unsigned operands, to prove the shared product selects the exact RV32M result.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 321.75, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -6.54, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 13.76, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 133.48, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10988, \\\"ff\\\": 1931, \\\"seeds\\\": [122.44, 133.48, 141.48], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T14:03:34.473639Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 4}\\n12:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r4s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Two-entry instruction skid queue\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The CoreMark cosim injects roughly 22% instruction-bus backpressure, and\\\\nthe current front end turns every unready imem cycle into a full fetch and\\\\ndecode bubble. The successful branch work has already reduced redirect\\\\nwaste, so absorbing independent delivery stalls is now a larger structural\\\\nsource of lost issue slots.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The CoreMark cosim injects roughly 22% instruction-bus backpressure, and\\\\nthe current front end turns every unready imem cycle into a full fetch and\\\\ndecode bubble. The successful branch work has already reduced redirect\\\\nwaste, so absorbing independent delivery stalls is now a larger structural\\\\nsource of lost issue slots.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the combinational IF-to-ID payload with a two-entry, PC-tagged\\\\ninstruction skid queue. Fetch fills an empty queue slot whenever imem is\\\\nready while ID independently consumes the head, allowing a previously\\\\nfetched instruction to enter decode during a later imem stall. Each entry\\\\ncarries its predictor-selected successor so sequential prefetch remains\\\\ncorrect; EX and ID redirects synchronously invalidate younger queued\\\\nentries and restart fetch at the resolved target. This keeps the existing\\\\nsingle-retire pipeline and RVFI boundary intact while converting many\\\\nisolated zero-wait misses into no-bubble cycles.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 7, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 334.25, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -2.91, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 18.18, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 131.65, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 3e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 3938669, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 11431, \\\"ff\\\": 2123, \\\"seeds\\\": [131.13, 131.65, 137.1], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T14:11:15.845885Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 4}\\n13:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-003-r4s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Folded-PC BHT indexing\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The profitable 16-entry BHT currently indexes only PC[5:2], so branch\\\\nsites separated by 64-byte code regions can repeatedly overwrite the\\\\nsame two-bit counter. CoreMark has several small hot routines and loops,\\\\nmaking destructive direction aliasing a likely remaining source of\\\\nrecoveries after decode-stage branch resolution.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The profitable 16-entry BHT currently indexes only PC[5:2], so branch\\\\nsites separated by 64-byte code regions can repeatedly overwrite the\\\\nsame two-bit counter. CoreMark has several small hot routines and loops,\\\\nmaking destructive direction aliasing a likely remaining source of\\\\nrecoveries after decode-stage branch resolution.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the direct BHT index with a four-bit folded-PC hash, for example\\\\nPC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], for both lookup and resolved-branch training. This\\\\nretains the existing 16 counters, reset policy, direct B-immediate target\\\\npath, and JAL behavior, but distributes otherwise congruent branch PCs\\\\nacross the table. Four local XOR gates should be materially cheaper than\\\\nanother predictor state array or target lookup, while fewer alias-driven\\\\ndirection misses improve CoreMark IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Derive the shared lookup and training BHT indices from a folded PC hash instead of PC[5:2], retaining the counter table and direct-target prediction logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed branch sites with identical low PC index but opposite behavior to verify folded-index separation, correct training, saturation, recovery, and RVFI PC order.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Derive the shared lookup and training BHT indices from a folded PC hash instead of PC[5:2], retaining the counter table and direct-target prediction logic.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed branch sites with identical low PC index but opposite behavior to verify folded-index separation, correct training, saturation, recovery, and RVFI PC order.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 317.51, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -7.77, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 12.27, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 131.72, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10793, \\\"ff\\\": 1923, \\\"seeds\\\": [130.46, 147.58, 131.72], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T14:07:48.805697Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 4}\\n14:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Authoritative decode branch resolution\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current decode stage already compares fully bypassed branch operands and\\\\ncomputes the direct successor, yet EX repeats the branch comparison and\\\\ntarget calculation before registering the same RVFI pc_wdata result. This\\\\nduplicate conditional-control cone adds LUTs and routing to the EX/MEM\\\\nendpoint after the successful early-resolution optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current decode stage already compares fully bypassed branch operands and\\\\ncomputes the direct successor, yet EX repeats the branch comparison and\\\\ntarget calculation before registering the same RVFI pc_wdata result. This\\\\nduplicate conditional-control cone adds LUTs and routing to the EX/MEM\\\\nendpoint after the successful early-resolution optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Make the decode-stage branch decision authoritative for every legal\\\\nconditional branch once its operands are ready. Carry the resolved taken\\\\nbit, successor, and target-misalignment fault state through ID/EX so EX\\\\nselects the recorded result, trains the BHT from the recorded direction,\\\\nand preserves precise illegal/trap behavior without recomputing a branch\\\\ncomparator or PC-plus-immediate adder. This should shorten the EX control\\\\npath while retaining the existing load interlock and recovery semantics.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend the ID/EX payload with decode-resolved branch direction, successor, and misalignment metadata; remove obsolete EX/MEM branch-only payload fields.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Capture the fully bypassed conditional-branch outcome for legal ready branches, including the taken misaligned-target fault condition, alongside the existing early redirect result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace duplicated conditional-branch comparison and target generation with the carried decode result, preserving redirect priority, trap conversion, RVFI pc_wdata, and BHT training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Update EX/MEM bundle assumptions after removal of branch-only fields that are no longer consumed downstream.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed cases for bypassed taken and not-taken branches, load-dependent branch interlocks, misaligned taken targets, predictor training, and RVFI PC sequencing.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend the ID/EX payload with decode-resolved branch direction, successor, and misalignment metadata; remove obsolete EX/MEM branch-only payload fields.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Capture the fully bypassed conditional-branch outcome for legal ready branches, including the taken misaligned-target fault condition, alongside the existing early redirect result.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace duplicated conditional-branch comparison and target generation with the carried decode result, preserving redirect priority, trap conversion, RVFI pc_wdata, and BHT training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Update EX/MEM bundle assumptions after removal of branch-only fields that are no longer consumed downstream.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed cases for bypassed taken and not-taken branches, load-dependent branch interlocks, misaligned taken targets, predictor training, and RVFI PC sequencing.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 262.72, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -23.69, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -7.11, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 108.99, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10442, \\\"ff\\\": 1958, \\\"seeds\\\": [108.99, 110.06, 103.02], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T14:37:44.605648Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 5, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r5s0 (regression, -23.69%): Once branches are already resolved in ID, carrying a 32-bit successor plus direction and misalignment state through ID/EX only trades EX recomputation for wider registered routing without reducing CoreMark recovery bubbles, so duplicate control logic should remain unless post-route timing proves the payload is cheaper.\\\"}\\n15:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r5s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"One-entry decoupled store buffer\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Random dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage whenever a\\\\nstore reaches EX/MEM, even though a completed store has no register result\\\\nand most following CoreMark instructions are independent. The failed fetch\\\\nqueue showed that broad front-end buffering costs too much Fmax, so the\\\\nnext decoupling point should be off the critical fetch and execute paths.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Random dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage whenever a\\\\nstore reaches EX/MEM, even though a completed store has no register result\\\\nand most following CoreMark instructions are independent. The failed fetch\\\\nqueue showed that broad front-end buffering costs too much Fmax, so the\\\\nnext decoupling point should be off the critical fetch and execute paths.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Insert a one-entry write buffer between MEM and the dmem pins. A store may\\\\nretire into an empty buffer in one cycle even when dmemReady is low; the\\\\nbuffer holds its aligned address, replicated data, and byte enables until\\\\nthe bus accepts it. Loads and a second store wait until the older buffered\\\\nstore drains, preserving in-order memory visibility, while independent\\\\nALU/control instructions continue through the existing single-retire\\\\npipeline. This converts isolated store-side bus stalls into useful work\\\\nwithout lengthening the predictor lookup or EX arithmetic cone.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/store_buffer.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry valid/ready write buffer that captures an aligned store transaction, drives dmem until accepted, and exposes empty/drain state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Route stores through the buffer, permit an empty-buffer store to advance without dmemReady, and retain exact RVFI store address, mask, and data fields at retirement.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional store-side dmem freezes with buffer-full and ordered-load interlocks while retaining the existing load and redirect priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire store enqueue, buffer drain, dmem pins, and memory-order status through the existing MEM and hazard controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add randomized dmem-stall cases proving independent instructions advance behind a buffered store, younger loads and stores wait for drain, and RVFI/order/memory data remain exact.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/store_buffer.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry valid/ready write buffer that captures an aligned store transaction, drives dmem until accepted, and exposes empty/drain state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Route stores through the buffer, permit an empty-buffer store to advance without dmemReady, and retain exact RVFI store address, mask, and data fields at retirement.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional store-side dmem freezes with buffer-full and ordered-load interlocks while retaining the existing load and redirect priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire store enqueue, buffer drain, dmem pins, and memory-order status through the existing MEM and hazard controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add randomized dmem-stall cases proving independent instructions advance behind a buffered store, younger loads and stores wait for drain, and RVFI/order/memory data remain exact.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"placement_failed\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": \\\"placement_failed\\\", \\\"seeds\\\": [null, null, null], \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 5}\\n16:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-003-r5s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-stage BHT training\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Conditional branches are now resolved with current operands in ID, but the\\\\nBHT is still updated one stage later in EX. That leaves the predictor using\\\\nstale counter state for the next fetches after a direction change, despite\\\\nthe correct branch outcome already being available without another ALU.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Conditional branches are now resolved with current operands in ID, but the\\\\nBHT is still updated one stage later in EX. That leaves the predictor using\\\\nstale counter state for the next fetches after a direction change, despite\\\\nthe correct branch outcome already being available without another ALU.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Train the existing two-bit BHT directly from the validated, operand-ready\\\\ndecode-stage branch result and remove the redundant EX-to-predictor training\\\\npath. This advances counter updates by one cycle without changing BHT size,\\\\nindexing, reset policy, direct-target generation, or the fetch lookup cone.\\\\nIt should reduce short-loop and closely spaced alias recovery bubbles while\\\\npreserving the successful ID-stage redirect and EX fallback behavior.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose a valid, non-stalled decode-stage branch-training event carrying the resolved branch PC and direction, gated until operands are forwardable and the instruction is legal.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire decode-stage branch training to the existing predictor and remove the superseded EX-stage training connections while retaining all redirect priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove redundant BHT training outputs; keep branch execution, misalignment traps, resolved pc_next, and EX recovery for branches not resolved in ID.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the earlier committed decode-stage training event without altering the sixteen-entry counter lookup, direct JAL prediction, or fetch-critical prediction selection.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed back-to-back and aliasing branch cases proving that ID-stage training is visible at the next lookup, saturates correctly, and preserves redirect and RVFI PC ordering.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose a valid, non-stalled decode-stage branch-training event carrying the resolved branch PC and direction, gated until operands are forwardable and the instruction is legal.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire decode-stage branch training to the existing predictor and remove the superseded EX-stage training connections while retaining all redirect priorities.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove redundant BHT training outputs; keep branch execution, misalignment traps, resolved pc_next, and EX recovery for branches not resolved in ID.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Accept the earlier committed decode-stage training event without altering the sixteen-entry counter lookup, direct JAL prediction, or fetch-critical prediction selection.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add directed back-to-back and aliasing branch cases proving that ID-stage training is visible at the next lookup, saturates correctly, and preserves redirect and RVFI PC ordering.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 345.35, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.31, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 22.11, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 143.27, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10700, \\\"ff\\\": 1927, \\\"seeds\\\": [143.27, 132.68, 143.58], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T14:33:09.477998Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 5, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r5s2 (improvement, +0.31%): When a legal conditional branch is operand-ready in ID, training its two-bit BHT under the same capture/redirect gate removes a cycle of stale counter state for nearby loop branches and aliases without lengthening the fetch lookup cone.\\\"}\\n17:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Shared magnitude divide datapath\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\\\\nremainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\\\\nselectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\\\\neven though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The ALU currently describes separate signed and unsigned quotient and\\\\nremainder operators. Those four large combinational arithmetic cones are\\\\nselectable on every EX cycle, creating avoidable LUT and routing pressure\\\\neven though every RV32M divide operation needs only one result form.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the four DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with a shared magnitude\\\\nquotient/remainder datapath: derive operand magnitudes only for signed\\\\noperations, perform one unsigned divide and modulo pair, and restore the\\\\nquotient or remainder sign according to RV32M rules. Keep explicit\\\\ndivide-by-zero behavior and retain the magnitude-based INT_MIN/-1 results.\\\\nThis halves the divider-class operator count without changing latency,\\\\nforwarding, retirement, or the fetch-critical predictor path, so it should\\\\nimprove Tang Nano placement and Fmax while preserving CoreMark IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU vectors across signedness boundaries, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and randomized values to validate the shared datapath.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace four signed/unsigned DIV and REM expressions with one operation-selected magnitude quotient/remainder datapath; preserve the ALTOPS mappings and all RV32M zero-divisor and overflow semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_alu.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend exact DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU vectors across signedness boundaries, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, and randomized values to validate the shared datapath.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 348.63, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.95, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 23.27, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 144.63, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 8005, \\\"ff\\\": 1930, \\\"seeds\\\": [144.63, 143.91, 155.52], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T16:50:02.426456Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 6, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r6s0 (improvement, +0.95%): Sharing a single unsigned magnitude quotient/remainder cone across DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU modestly reduces divider LUT/routing pressure while preserving RV32M sign, zero-divisor, and INT_MIN/-1 behavior through explicit result restoration.\\\"}\\n18:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r6s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decode-stage JALR recovery\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Conditional branches already recover in decode, but every JALR still\\\\nreaches EX before the core discovers that sequential fetch is wrong. CoreMark\\\\nuses call and return control flow often enough that this leaves a repeated\\\\ntwo-slot recovery penalty after the BHT has removed most loop-branch waste.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Conditional branches already recover in decode, but every JALR still\\\\nreaches EX before the core discovers that sequential fetch is wrong. CoreMark\\\\nuses call and return control flow often enough that this leaves a repeated\\\\ntwo-slot recovery penalty after the BHT has removed most loop-branch waste.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Extend the existing decode-stage control-resolution path to legal JALR\\\\ninstructions. Reuse its EX/MEM/WB operand bypasses to calculate the masked\\\\nrs1+immediate target in ID and redirect one cycle before EX whenever the\\\\nsource is ready and the target is aligned. Carry a single generalized\\\\ncontrol-resolved bit into EX to suppress duplicate recovery; load-dependent\\\\nor misaligned JALRs retain the current EX path so their interlock and trap\\\\nsemantics stay exact. This changes recovery-stage topology without adding a\\\\ntarget lookup or return stack to the fetch-critical predictor cone.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generalize the existing ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID bit without widening the carried successor payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Resolve legal, operand-ready, aligned JALR targets with the existing decode bypass network and emit the existing early redirect interface for both branches and JALR.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Preserve JALR link-value and misalignment handling while suppressing EX recovery for a control transfer already redirected in decode.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the generalized decode control redirect through the existing fetch and redirect-priority paths without changing the predictor lookup cone.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Retain load-use and dmem-stall precedence while treating a decode-resolved JALR exactly like the existing one-slot decode branch recovery.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add independent, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned JALR cases covering recovery depth, link writeback, precise traps, and RVFI PC/order sequencing.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generalize the existing ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a contr