-PC recovery cone. The register file is explicitly write-first,\\\\nbut ID repeats a writeback address comparison and data mux for each branch\\\\nsource before applying the genuinely necessary MEM and EX bypasses.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Remove ID's redundant WB-to-branch operand bypass and its three writeback\\\\nports. The regfile already returns wb_w_data for a same-cycle matching read\\\\naddress, making branch_rs1/branch_rs2 identical before the remaining\\\\nage-prioritized MEM and EX overrides. This eliminates two 5-bit comparators,\\\\nzero-register tests, and 32-bit mux legs from the early branch-resolution\\\\ncone, improving Fmax without changing instruction scheduling, IPC, RVFI, or\\\\nbypass semantics.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Delete the redundant writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Delete the redundant writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 333.04, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -5.81, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 17.76, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 138.16, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7863, \\\"ff\\\": 1896, \\\"seeds\\\": [142.71, 138.16, 134.34], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T18:09:47.303217Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 11}\\n33:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r11s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Correct 30-bit word-PC spine\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The fetch PC, predicted successor, and carried retirement PCs are always\\\\ninstruction aligned, yet the core routes their invariant low two zero bits\\\\nand uses 32-bit adders in the timing-sensitive fetch and redirect paths.\\\\nThe prior word-PC attempt failed cosimulation because it retained an\\\\nencoded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The fetch PC, predicted successor, and carried retirement PCs are always\\\\ninstruction aligned, yet the core routes their invariant low two zero bits\\\\nand uses 32-bit adders in the timing-sensitive fetch and redirect paths.\\\\nThe prior word-PC attempt failed cosimulation because it retained an\\\\nencoded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Represent sequential fetch, direct-JAL prediction, conditional-branch\\\\nrecovery, and non-JALR resolved successors as 30-bit instruction-word\\\\naddresses. PC+4 becomes pc_word+1. Direct JAL must use exactly the signed\\\\nJ-immediate bits [31:2], and B targets exactly the signed B-immediate bits\\\\n[31:2], dropping both encoded invariant low bits; this corrects the failed\\\\nearlier conversion. Reconstruct byte PCs only at imem, AUIPC/link-data,\\\\nJALR's full-width target/alignment check, and RVFI boundaries. Narrowing\\\\nthe persistent PC feedback/routing cone should improve Fmax without adding\\\\nqueueing state or changing single-retirement behavior.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 140.48, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -60.27, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -50.33, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 58.28, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7923, \\\"ff\\\": 1906, \\\"seeds\\\": [58.1, 58.28, 61.98], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T18:13:43.138227Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 11}\\n34:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Aligned decode-stage JAL steering\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"test/test_pipeline.py\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 380.62, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 7.64, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 34.58, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 157.9, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4148503, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7729, \\\"ff\\\": 1910, \\\"seeds\\\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 11, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_branch_predictor.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"End-to-end pipeline tests for rtl/core.sv.\\n\\nDrives a minimal Python-side imem/dmem against the core's combinational\\nfetch/load model and captures RVFI retirements. Covers the §8 phase-2\\nacceptance set: forwarding (EX->EX, MEM->EX), branches, JAL, JALR,\\nSW+LW roundtrip, load-use stall, and the trap discipline (illegal /\\nECALL trap, EBREAK does NOT trap).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport cocotb\\nfrom cocotb.clock import Clock\\nfrom cocotb.triggers import RisingEdge, Timer\\n\\nfrom _helpers import run_cocotb\\n\\n\\n# ── RV32I instruction encoder helpers ──────────────────────────────────────\\ndef _r(funct7, rs2, rs1, funct3, rd, opcode):\\n    return ((funct7 & 0x7F) << 25) | ((rs2 & 0x1F) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) \\\\\\n         | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) | ((rd & 0x1F) << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n\\n\\ndef _i(imm, rs1, funct3, rd, opcode):\\n    return ((imm & 0xFFF) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) \\\\\\n         | ((rd & 0x1F) << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n\\n\\ndef _s(imm, rs2, rs1, funct3, opcode):\\n    imm_hi = (imm >> 5) & 0x7F\\n    imm_lo = imm & 0x1F\\n    return (imm_hi << 25) | ((rs2 & 0x1F) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) \\\\\\n         | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) | (imm_lo << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n\\n\\ndef _b(imm, rs2, rs1, funct3, opcode):\\n    # imm is a 13-bit signed number; bit 0 is implicitly zero.\\n    b12  = (imm >> 12) & 1\\n    b105 = (imm >> 5)  & 0x3F\\n    b41  = (imm >> 1)  & 0xF\\n    b11  = (imm >> 11) & 1\\n    return (b12 << 31) | (b105 << 25) | ((rs2 & 0x1F) << 20) | ((rs1 & 0x1F) << 15) \\\\\\n         | ((funct3 & 0x7) << 12) | (b41 << 8) | (b11 << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n\\n\\ndef _j(imm, rd, opcode):\\n    # 21-bit signed imm; bit 0 implicit zero.\\n    b20    = (imm >> 20) & 1\\n    b101   = (imm >> 1)  & 0x3FF\\n    b11    = (imm >> 11) & 1\\n    b1912  = (imm >> 12) & 0xFF\\n    return (b20 << 31) | (b101 << 21) | (b11 << 20) | (b1912 << 12) \\\\\\n         | ((rd & 0x1F) << 7) | (opcode & 0x7F)\\n\\n\\ndef ADDI(rd, rs1, imm): return _i(imm & 0xFFF, rs1, 0b000, rd, 0b0010011)\\ndef ADD (rd, rs1, rs2): return _r(0, rs2, rs1, 0b000, rd, 0b0110011)\\ndef LW  (rd, rs1, imm): return _i(imm & 0xFFF, rs1, 0b010, rd, 0b0000011)\\ndef SW  (rs2, rs1, imm): return _s(imm & 0xFFF, rs2, rs1, 0b010, 0b0100011)\\ndef BEQ (rs1, rs2, imm): return _b(imm, rs2, rs1, 0b000, 0b1100011)\\ndef JAL (rd, imm):       return _j(imm, rd, 0b1101111)\\ndef JALR(rd, rs1, imm):  return _i(imm & 0xFFF, rs1, 0b000, rd, 0b1100111)\\ndef NOP():               return ADDI(0, 0, 0)        # = 0x00000013\\ndef EBREAK():            return 0x00100073\\ndef ECALL():             return 0x00000073\\n\\n\\n# ── Harness ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\nasync def _run(dut, program, dmem_init=None, max_cycles=200, ready=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Drive imem/dmem; capture RVFI retirements until EBREAK or max_cycles.\\n\\n    imem is read combinationally each cycle from imemAddr; dmem similarly.\\n    Stores get applied to the Python-side dmem dict so subsequent loads\\n    see the new value.\\n\\n    Returns (retirements, dmem) where retirements is a list of dicts\\n    sampled on every cycle that rvfi_valid=1.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    imem = {i * 4: instr & 0xFFFFFFFF for i, instr in enumerate(program)}\\n    dmem = dict(dmem_init or {})\\n    retirements: list[dict] = []\\n\\n    cocotb.start_soon(Clock(dut.clock, 10, \\\"ns\\\").start())\\n\\n    dut.reset.value = 1\\n    dut.io_imemData.value = 0\\n    dut.io_dmemRData.value = 0\\n    # Zero-wait by default; individual tests may schedule imem/dmem stalls\\n    # with ready(cycle) -> (imem_ready, dmem_ready).\\n    dut.io_imemReady.value = 1\\n    dut.io_dmemReady.value = 1\\n    for _ in range(3):\\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\\n\\n    # Deassert reset and prime the imem read for the first PC=0 fetch.\\n    dut.reset.value = 0\\n    dut.io_imemData.value = imem.get(0, EBREAK())\\n\\n    for cycle in range(max_cycles):\\n        if ready is None:\\n            imem_ready, dmem_ready = 1, 1\\n        else:\\n            imem_ready, dmem_ready = ready(cycle)\\n        dut.io_imemReady.value = imem_ready\\n        dut.io_dmemReady.value = dmem_ready\\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\\n        await Timer(1, \\\"ns\\\")  # let combinational signals settle\\n\\n        # Sample the post-edge state.\\n        ia        = int(dut.io_imemAddr.value)\\n        da        = int(dut.io_dmemAddr.value)\\n        wen       = int(dut.io_dmemWEn.value)\\n        rvfi_v    = int(dut.io_rvfi_valid_0.value)\\n\\n        # Apply dmem write side effects.\\n        if wen:\\n            wdata = int(dut.io_dmemWData.value)\\n            wa = da & ~3\\n            old = dmem.get(wa, 0)\\n            new = old\\n            for i in range(4):\\n                if (wen >> i) & 1:\\n                    bv = (wdata >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF\\n                    new = (new & ~(0xFF << (i * 8))) | (bv << (i * 8))\\n            dmem[wa] = new\\n\\n        # Capture RVFI retirement.\\n        if rvfi_v:\\n            r = {\\n                \\\"order\\\":     int(dut.io_rvfi_order_0.value),\\n                \\\"insn\\\":      int(dut.io_rvfi_insn_0.value),\\n                \\\"pc\\\":        int(dut.io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"pc_next\\\":   int(dut.io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"rd\\\":        int(dut.io_rvfi_rd_addr_0.value),\\n                \\\"rd_wdata\\\":  int(dut.io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"rs1_addr\\\":  int(dut.io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0.value),\\n                \\\"rs1_rdata\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"rs2_addr\\\":  int(dut.io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0.value),\\n                \\\"rs2_rdata\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"trap\\\":      int(dut.io_rvfi_trap_0.value),\\n                \\\"mem_addr\\\":  int(dut.io_rvfi_mem_addr_0.value),\\n                \\\"mem_wmask\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0.value),\\n                \\\"mem_wdata\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"mem_rmask\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0.value),\\n                \\\"mem_rdata\\\": int(dut.io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0.value),\\n                \\\"cycle\\\":     cycle,\\n            }\\n            retirements.append(r)\\n            if r[\\\"insn\\\"] == EBREAK():\\n                break\\n\\n        # Drive next cycle's imem fetch and dmem read combinationally.\\n        dut.io_imemData.value  = imem.get(ia & ~3, EBREAK())\\n        dut.io_dmemRData.value = dmem.get(da & ~3, 0)\\n    else:\\n        raise AssertionError(f\\\"max_cycles={max_cycles} reached without EBREAK\\\")\\n\\n    return retirements, dmem\\n\\n\\ndef _by_insn(retirements, insn):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return all retirements matching a specific instruction word.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [r for r in retirements if r[\\\"insn\\\"] == insn]\\n\\n\\n# ── Tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n@cocotb.test()\\nasync def forwarding_ex_to_ex(dut):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"ADDI x1, x0, 5; ADDI x2, x1, 3 — back-to-back rs1 forward from EX/MEM.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    program = [ADDI(1, 0, 5), ADDI(2, 1, 3), EBREAK()]\\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program)\\n    [r1] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(1, 0, 5))\\n    [r2] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(2, 1, 3))\\n    assert r1[\\\"rd\\\"] == 1 and r1[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] == 5\\n    assert r2[\\\"rd\\\"] == 2 and r2[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] == 8, (\\n        f\\\"x2 should be x1+3=8 via EX->EX forward, got 0x{r2['rd_wdata']:08x}\\\"\\n    )\\n    # Order must be strict +1.\\n    orders = [r[\\\"order\\\"] for r in rets]\\n    assert orders == list(range(orders[0], orders[0] + len(rets)))\\n\\n\\n@cocotb.test()\\nasync def forwarding_mem_to_ex(dut):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"ADDI x1, x0, 5; NOP; ADDI x2, x1, 3 — rs1 forward from MEM/WB stage.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    program = [ADDI(1, 0, 5), NOP(), ADDI(2, 1, 3), EBREAK()]\\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program)\\n    [r2] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(2, 1, 3))\\n    assert r2[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] == 8\\n\\n\\n@cocotb.test()\\nasync def load_use_stalls(dut):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"SW x3 to mem; LW x1, 0(x0); ADD x2, x1, x4 — load-use must stall once.\\n\\n    All immediates kept inside the signed 12-bit positive range so ADDI's\\n    sign-extension doesn't muddy the expected values.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    program = [\\n        ADDI(3, 0, 0x123),     # x3 = 0x123\\n        ADDI(4, 0, 0x100),     # x4 = 0x100\\n        SW  (3, 0, 0),         # mem[0] = x3\\n        LW  (1, 0, 0),         # x1 = mem[0]; uses x1 next cycle -> stall\\n        ADD (2, 1, 4),         # x2 = x1 + x4 = 0x223\\n        EBREAK(),\\n    ]\\n    rets, dmem = await _run(dut, program)\\n    [r2] = _by_insn(rets, ADD(2, 1, 4))\\n    assert r2[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] == 0x223, f\\\"x2 expected 0x223, got 0x{r2['rd_wdata']:08x}\\\"\\n    assert dmem[0] == 0x123, f\\\"mem[0] should hold 0x123, got {dmem[0]:#x}\\\"\\n\\n\\n@cocotb.test()\\nasync def branch_taken_skips(dut):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"BEQ x0, x0, +8 — the wrong-path instruction must NOT retire at all,\\n    not merely retire with rd_wdata != 99. Asserting only the side effect\\n    would let a wrong-path retirement with rd=0 / trap=1 / different data\\n    pass silently.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    program = [\\n        BEQ(0, 0, 8),          # PC=0;  taken; skip the next instr\\n        ADDI(1, 0, 99),        # PC=4;  SHOULD NEVER retire\\n        ADDI(2, 0, 42),        # PC=8;  branch target\\n        EBREAK(),\\n    ]\\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program)\\n    # Strict: no retirement should originate from PC=4.\\n    leaked = [r for r in rets if r[\\\"pc\\\"] == 4]\\n    assert not leaked, f\\\"wrong-path retirement leaked from PC=4: {leaked}\\\"\\n    # Strict: no retirement carries the skipped instruction word at all.\\n    leaked_insn = [r for r in rets if r[\\\"insn\\\"] == ADDI(1, 0, 99)]\\n    assert not leaked_insn, f\\\"skipped instr ADDI x1,99 retired: {leaked_insn}\\\"\\n    # Sanity: the target instruction and the EBREAK do retire, in order.\\n    pcs = [r[\\\"pc\\\"] for r in rets]\\n    assert pcs == [0, 8, 12], f\\\"unexpected retirement PC sequence: {pcs}\\\"\\n    [r2] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(2, 0, 42))\\n    assert r2[\\\"rd_wdata\\\"] == 42\\n    [branch] = _by_insn(rets, BEQ(0, 0, 8))\\n    assert branch[\\\"pc_next\\\"] == 8\\n    assert r2[\\\"cycle\\\"] == branch[\\\"cycle\\\"] + 1, (\\n        \\\"an ID-resolved independent branch should feed its target without \\\"\\n        \\\"an EX-recovery retirement bubble\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\n@cocotb.test()\\nasync def branch_not_taken_remains_sequential(dut):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A not-taken conditional branch uses fetch's PC+4 without recovery.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    branch = BEQ(0, 1, 8)\\n    program = [\\n        ADDI(1, 0, 1),\\n        branch,\\n        ADDI(2, 0, 42),\\n        EBREAK(),\\n    ]\\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program)\\n    assert [r[\\\"pc\\\"] for r in rets] == [0, 4, 8, 12]\\n    [br] = _by_insn(rets, branch)\\n    [fallthrough] = _by_insn(rets, ADDI(2, 0, 42))\\n    assert br[\\\"pc_next\\\"] == 8\\n    assert fallthrough[\\\"cycle\\\"] == br[\\\"cycle\\\"] + 1\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files cores/bench | rg -i '(timing|report|nextpnr|route|json)\\\"'$'\\\"' | head -80 && find cores/bench -maxdepth 3 -type f \\\\\\\\( -name '*.json' -o -name '*.rpt' -o -name '*.log' \\\\\\\\) -print | head -80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files cores/bench | rg -i '(timing|report|nextpnr|route|json)\\\"'$'\\\"' | head -80 && find cores/bench -maxdepth 3 -type f \\\\\\\\( -name '*.json' -o -name '*.rpt' -o -name '*.log' \\\\\\\\) -print | head -80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed2/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed2/pnr.json\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed3/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed3/pnr.json\\ncores/bench/generated/synth.json\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed1/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed1/pnr.json\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r12s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r4s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r6s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r4s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r9s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r6s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r2s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r2s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-005-r12s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r8s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r5s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-