": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so their bypass muxes participate in\\nthe decode-to-PC recovery cone. The register file is explicitly write-first,\\nbut ID repeats a writeback address comparison and data mux for each branch\\nsource before applying the genuinely necessary MEM and EX bypasses.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so their bypass muxes participate in\\nthe decode-to-PC recovery cone. The register file is explicitly write-first,\\nbut ID repeats a writeback address comparison and data mux for each branch\\nsource before applying the genuinely necessary MEM and EX bypasses.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove ID's redundant WB-to-branch operand bypass and its three writeback\\nports. The regfile already returns wb_w_data for a same-cycle matching read\\naddress, making branch_rs1/branch_rs2 identical before the remaining\\nage-prioritized MEM and EX overrides. This eliminates two 5-bit comparators,\\nzero-register tests, and 32-bit mux legs from the early branch-resolution\\ncone, improving Fmax without changing instruction scheduling, IPC, RVFI, or\\nbypass semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the redundant writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \