ded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Represent sequential fetch, direct-JAL prediction, conditional-branch\\nrecovery, and non-JALR resolved successors as 30-bit instruction-word\\naddresses. PC+4 becomes pc_word+1. Direct JAL must use exactly the signed\\nJ-immediate bits [31:2], and B targets exactly the signed B-immediate bits\\n[31:2], dropping both encoded invariant low bits; this corrects the failed\\nearlier conversion. Reconstruct byte PCs only at imem, AUIPC/link-data,\\nJALR's full-width target/alignment check, and RVFI boundaries. Narrowing\\nthe persistent PC feedback/routing cone should improve Fmax without adding\\nqueueing state or changing single-retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the inte