{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\\\") | {id,title,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,lut4,ff,hypothesis}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\nrg -n 'worktree|source_id|hyp-20260711-003-r11s2|current' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/core.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Aligned decode-stage JAL steering\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 380.62,\n  \"delta_pct\": 7.64,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9,\n  \"lut4\": 7729,\n  \"ff\": 1910,\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 4,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\ncores/bench/core.yaml:13:current:\ncores/bench/core.yaml:19:  source_id: hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative divide execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": 