t match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the\\nload-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads\\nthe matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store,\\nJALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in\\nCoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, or retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed immediate-alias-after-load cases that must advance without a bubble, plus true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies that must still interlock and retire correctly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\