 every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 380.62, \"delta_pct\": 7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7729, \"ff\": 1910, \"seeds\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Share execute control target adders\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic independently builds the same PC-relative\\ntarget for branches and direct JALs, and builds a second rs1-plus-immediate\\nadder for JALR even though its ALU operation is already ADD. These duplicate\\narithmetic cones consume LUTs and routing at the EX/MEM timing endpoint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic independently builds the same PC-relative\\ntarget for branches and direct JALs, and builds a second rs1-plus-immediate\\nadder for JALR even though its ALU operation is already ADD. These duplicate\\narithmetic cones consume LUTs and routing at the EX/MEM timing endpoint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Refactor EX control-target generation to compute PC+4 and PC+immediate once\\nper instruction, use the latter for both branch and direct-JAL resolution,\\nand derive the JALR sum from the existing ALU result. This removes duplicate\\n32-bit adders without adding state, changing any redirect timing, or\\nchanging the carried RVFI data, so CoreMark IPC should remain unchanged\\nwhile Tang Nano placement and Fmax improve.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Share PC+4 and PC-relative target arithmetic across branch and JAL control paths, and reuse the ADD-class ALU result for the JALR target before bit-zero clearing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed branch, JAL, JALR, and misaligned-control cases that verify successor PCs, link data, trap behavior, redirect priority, and RVFI retirement order after adder sharing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Share PC+4 and PC-relative target arithmetic across branch and JAL control paths, and reuse the ADD-class ALU result for the JALR target before bit-zero clearing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed branch, JAL, JALR, and misaligned-control cases that verify successor PCs, link data, trap behavior, redirect priority, and RVFI retirement order after adder sharing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 323.42, \"delta_pct\": -15.03, \"vs_baseline\": 14.36, \"fmax_mhz\": 134.17, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8269, \"ff\": 1918, \"seeds\": [134.17, 143.35, 122.14], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:03:16.160065Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:36:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-005-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Registered fetch decode boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current IF/ID payload is combinational, so an instruction-memory read\\ncan feed decoder/control logic and then steer the next PC in the same clock\\ninterval. The earlier two-entry queue reduced stall cycles but its ready,\\nflush, and occupancy logic reduced Fmax more than that IPC benefit repaid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current IF/ID payload is combinational, so an instruction-memory read\\ncan feed decoder/control logic and then steer the next PC in the same clock\\ninterval. The earlier two-entry queue reduced stall cycles but its ready,\\nflush, and occupancy logic reduced Fmax more than that IPC benefit repaid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational IF/ID handoff with one registered, valid-tagged\\nfetch buffer that is consumed every cycle by decode. This deliberately\\navoids a queue, prefetch policy, or predictor lookup: when the buffer is\\nconsumed and imem is ready, fetch refills it in the same edge. Decode-stage\\nbranch and direct-JAL resolution remains intact, with redirects invalidating\\nthe younger refill and winning over all fetch enables. Breaking the\\nimem-to-decode-to-PC feedback path should raise Tang Nano Fmax enough to\\noffset the extra recovery slot on control transfers while preserving\\nsingle-retirement RVFI ordering and all bus-stall behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Make the IF/ID payload an explicitly registered fetch-buffer bundle with a valid bit and its sequential-successor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry IF/ID register, refill it from imem on a ready cycle, and give older EX and decode redirects priority over stale-buffer capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the registered fetch payload while retaining existing decode-stage branch/JAL steering, operand bypasses, and capturable-control gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust stall and flush generation for fetch-buffer consume/refill so imem and dmem backpressure cannot duplicate, drop, or replay instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire registered IF/ID validity and fetch-buffer control through the pipeline without changing the external imem, dmem, or RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed refill, imem-stall, load-use, branch/JAL redirect, and redirect-during-stall tests that check exact RVFI retirement order and PCs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Make the IF/ID payload an explicitly registered fetch-buffer bundle with a valid bit and its sequential-successor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry IF/ID register, refill it from imem on a ready cycle, and give older EX and decode redirects priority over stale-buffer capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the registered fetch payload while retaining existing decode-stage branch/JAL steering, operand bypasses, and capturable-control gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust stall and flush generation for fetch-buffer consume/refill so imem and dmem backpressure cannot duplicate, drop, or replay instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire registered IF/ID validity and fetch-buffer control through the pipeline without changing the external imem, dmem, or RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed refill, imem-stall, load-use, branch/JAL redirect, and redirect-during-stall tests that check exact RVFI retirement order and PCs.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 372.83, \"delta_pct\": -2.05, \"vs_baseline\": 31.83, \"fmax_mhz\": 166.36, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4462141, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7816, \"ff\": 2027, \"seeds\": [157.04, 166.36, 176.09], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:09:59.084126Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-005-r12s1 (regression, -2.05%): A one-entry valid-tagged registered IF/ID buffer can regress CoreMark when its compulsory control-transfer recovery slot and refill/redirect control outweigh the timing relief from cutting the imem-to-decode-to-PC combinational path.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-006-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Elide sequential predictor metadata\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current best core intentionally predicts only PC+4 in fetch, while\\nlegal conditional branches and direct JALs steer from ID. Nevertheless it\\ntransports a 32-bit predicted-next-PC through IF/ID and ID/EX solely to\\nrepresent that invariant sequential successor, adding wide routing and\\nregister load to the control path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best core intentionally predicts only PC+4 in fetch, while\\nlegal conditional branches and direct JALs steer from ID. Nevertheless it\\ntransports a 32-bit predicted-next-PC through IF/ID and ID/EX solely to\\nrepresent that invariant sequential successor, adding wide routing and\\nregister load to the control path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the sequential predictor implicit rather than carried metadata.\\nRemove predicted_next_pc from the fetch and ID/EX bundles and eliminate\\nthe standalone predictor wiring. IF advances by its local PC+4 default;\\nID determines whether its already-computed branch/JAL successor differs\\nfrom local PC+4, and EX uses the same local comparison only for unresolved\\nJALR recovery. The existing control_resolved_id marker continues to\\nsuppress duplicate EX redirects. This keeps the proven no-table,\\nno-target-adder fetch policy, but removes a redundant 32-bit pipeline\\npayload and its fanout without weakening alignment, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant predicted_next_pc members from IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Retire the standalone always-sequential lookup interface, or reduce it to local sequential-policy documentation if the source file remains.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate the PC+4 sequential successor locally while retaining older-EX and ID redirect priority over stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare decode-resolved branch and JAL successors against local PC+4 instead of carried predictor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"For unresolved JALR recovery, compare the resolved successor with local PC+4; preserve the decode-resolution suppression and all trap paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the obsolete predictor instance and predicted-successor wiring while preserving the external imem, dmem, and RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover sequential fall-through, ID-resolved branch and JAL steering, JALR recovery, redirect-over-stall priority, and RVFI PC sequencing after metadata removal.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant predicted_next_pc members from IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Retire the standalone always-sequential lookup interface, or reduce it to local sequential-policy documentation if the source file remains.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate the PC+4 sequential successor locally while retaining older-EX and ID redirect priority over stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare decode-resolved branch and JAL successors against local PC+4 instead of carried predictor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"For unresolved JALR recovery, compare the resolved successor with local PC+4; preserve the decode-resolution suppression and all trap paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the obsolete predictor instance and predicted-successor wiring while preserving the external imem, dmem, and RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover sequential fall-through, ID-resolved branch and JAL steering, JALR recovery, redirect-over-stall priority, and RVFI PC sequencing after metadata removal.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 186.69, \"delta_pct\": -50.95, \"vs_baseline\": -33.99, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.45, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7762, \"ff\": 1871, \"seeds\": [77.36, 80.31, 77.45], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:07:11.863783Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-006-r12s2 (regression, -50.95%): Even an invariant PC+4 successor is valuable registered metadata: recomputing `in.pc + 4` in both ID and EX redirect comparisons adds 32-bit arithmetic to recovery control cones, so payload elision must not trade routing for repeated critical-path computation without post-route evidence.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:38:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Validated load-use source qualification\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a load destination with both\\narbitrary source-field bit slices of every following instruction. CoreMark\\ncontains many immediate, U-type, and direct-JAL instructions whose encoded\\nrs2 or both source fields are not read, so aliases create avoidable bubbles\\nduring the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock currently compares a load destination with both\\narbitrary source-field bit slices of every following instruction. CoreMark\\ncontains many immediate, U-type, and direct-JAL instructions whose encoded\\nrs2 or both source fields are not read, so aliases create avoidable bubbles\\nduring the measured loop.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add decoder-produced rs1/rs2-read qualifiers that default conservatively to\\nasserted and are cleared only inside the same fully validated legal decode\\narms that clear is_illegal. Gate each load-use comparison with its matching\\nqualifier. This preserves the existing conservative dependency behavior for\\nevery reserved or illegal encoding (the failure mode of prior qualifier\\nattempts), while removing bubbles only for proven source-free fields of\\nlegal OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE, EBREAK, and JAL instructions.\\nNo forwarding, bus timing, or retirement behavior changes; higher useful IPC\\nshould improve CoreMark fitness without lengthening fetch control logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose rs1/rs2-use qualifiers, default both asserted, and deassert them only in the already validated legal decode arms according to each instruction's architectural source use.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the decoder's validated source-use outputs alongside decode so hazard logic receives qualifiers for the current IF/ID instruction without altering operand or RVFI capture behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with its corresponding validated source-use qualifier while keeping all existing load, redirect, and memory-backpressure priority rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decode-stage source-use qualifiers to the load-use interlock without changing the external memory or single-channel RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add immediate-field alias cases after loads for legal source-free forms, plus reserved encodings and real rs1/rs2 dependencies, checking stalls, register values, traps, and RVFI order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose rs1/rs2-use qualifiers, default both asserted, and deassert them only in the already validated legal decode arms according to each instruction's architectural source use.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the decoder's validated source-use outputs alongside decode so hazard logic receives qualifiers for the current IF/ID instruction without altering operand or RVFI capture behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each load-use register comparison with its corresponding validated source-use qualifier while keeping all existing load, redirect, and memory-backpressure priority rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the decode-stage source-use qualifiers to the load-use interlock without changing the external memory or single-channel RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add immediate-field alias cases after loads for legal source-free forms, plus reserved encodings and real rs1/rs2 dependencies, checking stalls, register values, traps, and RVFI order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\n: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:14 (14)\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:11 (11)\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\nSBY 16:17:47 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_60 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 16:17:47 [r