lta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 302.55, \"delta_pct\": 6.98, \"vs_baseline\": 6.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Decode-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector presently compares a pending load destination against\\nboth instruction bit fields [19:15] and [24:20] unconditionally. Many\\nRV32I encodings use one or both fields as immediate bits rather than source\\nregisters, so an accidental bit match inserts a needless pipeline bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Carry explicit rs1/rs2-use qualification from the validated decoder to the\\nload-use interlock. Stall only when the following instruction truly reads\\nthe matching source register; retain stalls for real ALU, branch, store,\\nJALR, and address dependencies. This removes false post-load bubbles in\\nCoreMark's immediate-heavy code without changing pipeline depth, forwarding,\\nmemory timing, or retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 decode signals, with both false by default and set only for instruction forms that architecturally consume each operand.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoder's source-use qualification alongside the decode-stage register fields for hazard detection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode-aware source-use signals from ID to the load-use hazard unit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate each pending-load register comparison by whether the fetched instruction truly reads that source, while preserving existing stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.p