ly for the exact canonical return\\nencoding `jalr x0, x1, 0` when no older EX or MEM writer targets x1. Its target\\nis the clean regfile x1 value with bit zero cleared, so this path needs neither\\noperand-bypass muxes nor a 32-bit add. If x1 is pending, the target is\\nmisaligned, or the pipeline is stalled, retain normal EX-stage JALR recovery\\nand trap behavior. This can recover common leaf/helper returns without adding\\nstate or lengthening the fetch predictor cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-resolved canonical return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only jalr x0,x1,0; conservatively require x1 not to be pending in EX or MEM, form the target as the aligned clean regfile value, and issue a decode redirect only for an aligned capturable return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried return-resolved marker to avoid duplicate recovery while retaining full JALR target, link, forwarding, and misalignment-trap behavior for every other case.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow decode return redirect through the existing older-EX redirect priority without changing the JAL-only fetch predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add clean-register canonical-return, pending-x1 fallback, and misaligned-return tests that check redirect timing, RVFI PC/order, link semantics, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-resolved canonical return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only jalr x0,x1,0; conservatively require x1 not to be pending in EX or MEM, form the target as the aligned clean regfile value, and issue a decode redirect only for an aligned capturable return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried return-resolved marker to avoid duplicate recovery while retaining full JALR target, link, forwarding, and misalignment-trap behavior for every other case.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow decode return redirect through the existing older-EX redirect priority without changing the JAL-only fetch predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add clean-register canonical-return, pending-x1 fallback, and misaligned-return tests that check redirect timing, RVFI PC/order, link semantics, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 279.44, \"delta_pct\": -20.97, \"vs_baseline\": -1.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.58, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4136096, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8118, \"ff\": 1898, \"seeds\": [115.58, 118.23, 111.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:47:27.432814Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.97%): Even a bypass-free `jalr x0, x1, 0` decode redirect regresses CoreMark when x1-pending comparisons, target alignment gating, and the ID early-redirect selection add control/routing cost that common return bubbles cannot amortize, so canonical-return recovery should remain in EX unless its decode path is demonstrably cheaper post-route.\"}\n29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Register-slice the RVFI retirement bundle\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The FPGA benchmark deliberately XOR-reduces every RVFI output into the LED,\\nso the complete retirement payload remains a live, high-fanout timing cone.\\nToday fields from MEM/WB and the combinational writeback mux drive that\\nexternal reduction directly, even though RVFI consumers only require an\\nordered stream of architectural retirements rather than zero extra latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The FPGA benchmark deliberately XOR-reduces every RVFI output into the LED,\\nso the complete retirement payload remains a live, high-fanout timing cone.\\nToday fields from MEM/WB and the combinational writeback mux drive that\\nexternal reduction directly, even though RVFI consumers only require an\\nordered stream of architectural retirements rather than zero extra latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one dedicated RVFI output register in core.sv. Capture every channel-0\\nRVFI field and the current order value atomically when MEM/WB retires, then\\ndrive the top-level ports solely from that register. The extra fixed\\nobservation cycle leaves execution, marker timing, and retirement order\\nunchanged while cutting the MEM/WB/writeback-to-wrapper fanout path. This\\nshould improve placed Fmax without extending fetch, ALU, memory, or branch\\ntiming cones.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce an atomically captured channel-0 RVFI register, delay valid and all payload fields together by one observation cycle, and preserve contiguous order generation from MEM/WB retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add retirement-stream checks proving the registered RVFI bundle preserves field coherence, strict order, bubbles, memory masks, and the final EBREAK record despite the fixed output delay.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce an atomically captured channel-0 RVFI register, delay valid and all payload fields together by one observation cycle, and preserve contiguous order generation from MEM/WB retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add retirement-stream checks proving the registered RVFI bundle preserves field coherence, strict order, bubbles, memory masks, and the final EBREAK record despite the fixed output delay.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 147.88, \"delta_pct\": -58.18, \"vs_baseline\": -47.71, \"fmax_mhz\": 61.35, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7863, \"ff\": 2249, \"seeds\": [61.35, 64.4, 61.32], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:57:33.390502Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r10s0 (regression, -58.18%): Registering the entire RVFI retirement payload can lose badly on this FPGA because the added wide bundle of flip-flops and routing outweighs any relief from removing MEM/WB and writeback-mux fanout, so high-fanout observability logic needs post-route validation before adding a full-width pipeline stage.\"}\n30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Word-addressed control-flow spine\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current core carries byte-addressed 32-bit PCs through every pipeline\\nbundle and repeatedly performs PC+4 and PC+immediate arithmetic in fetch,\\ndecode, and execute. RV32I instructions are always four-byte aligned, so\\nthe two low PC bits are invariant zeros on every architecturally executed\\npath. The current JAL-only prediction makes this PC feedback path more\\nimportant to routed Fmax than the removed conditional-BHT logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core carries byte-addressed 32-bit PCs through every pipeline\\nbundle and repeatedly performs PC+4 and PC+immediate arithmetic in fetch,\\ndecode, and execute. RV32I instructions are always four-byte aligned, so\\nthe two low PC bits are invariant zeros on every architecturally executed\\npath. The current JAL-only prediction makes this PC feedback path more\\nimportant to routed Fmax than the removed conditional-BHT logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Rebuild the control-flow spine around a 30-bit word PC internally. Fetch,\\ndirect-JAL prediction, decode-stage branch recovery, and EX branch/JAL\\ntarget generation operate on pc_word plus signed immediate[31:2]; pipeline\\nbundles carry word PCs and word successors. Reconstruct {pc_word,2'b00}\\nonly where an architectural byte address is required (imem, AUIPC/link\\ndata, dmem-derived RVFI context, and RVFI pc fields). JALR retains a\\nfull-width sum solely for its mandated bit-0 clear and bit-1 misalignment\\ntrap. This removes invariant low-bit routing and narrows the pervasive\\nsequential/relative-target adders without changing retirement width,\\nredirect priority, trap rules, or external I/O.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace pipeline PC and successor members with 30-bit word-address representations, retaining helpers or documented reconstruction points for architectural 32-bit PC values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store a word-addressed fetch PC, form imemAddr by appending two zero bits, and perform sequential/direct-JAL next-PC selection in word units while retaining redirect-over-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept and return word PCs, derive the signed JAL word displacement from immediate[31:2], and avoid speculating an instruction-address-misaligned JAL target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Calculate legal operand-ready conditional branch targets and decode redirects in word units, while preserving the existing forwarded compare and misaligned-target trap handoff.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for AUIPC, branch, JAL, link, and resolved successor paths; retain a full JALR sum for exact alignment semantics and materialize byte PCs only for architectural data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the narrower PC payload unchanged through MEM/WB without altering load/store handling or RVFI memory fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Reconstruct full byte PCs and successors at RVFI channel 0, keeping rvfi_order, trap, and all top-level interface fields unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed forward and backward control-flow cases near word-PC wrap, plus aligned and misaligned branch/JAL/JALR checks for RVFI pc_rdata, pc_wdata, trap, and retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace pipeline PC and successor members with 30-bit word-address representations, retaining helpers or documented reconstruction points for architectural 32-bit PC values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store a word-addressed fetch PC, form imemAddr by appending two zero bits, and perform sequential/direct-JAL next-PC selection in word units while retaining redirect-over-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept and return word PCs, derive the signed JAL word displacement from immediate[31:2], and avoid speculating an instruction-address-misaligned JAL target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Calculate legal operand-ready conditional branch targets and decode redirects in word units, while preserving the existing forwarded compare and misaligned-target trap handoff.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for AUIPC, branch, JAL, link, and resolved successor paths; retain a full JALR sum for exact alignment semantics and materialize byte PCs only for architectural 