irect that reuses the existing ID redirect priority and target path.\\nJAL has no source dependency, so its legal aligned target can steer the PC\\non the edge that captures the JAL into ID/EX, preserving the current\\nno-bubble control-flow behavior. Carry a decode-resolved control marker to\\nsuppress EX's duplicate JAL recovery; leave misaligned JAL targets on the\\nexisting EX trap path. This removes J-immediate extraction, target addition,\\nand the predictor mux from the fetch-critical path while avoiding the bypass,\\npending-register, and indirect-target logic that made return fast paths lose.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction so the sequential successor is the only fetch prediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate the sequential predicted successor locally and retain the existing higher-priority decode and EX redirect handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the legal aligned decode control-flow resolver to issue a direct-JAL redirect and carry a marker that EX must not recover it again.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX early-resolution metadata from conditional-branch-only state to decoded direct-control-flow state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress duplicate recovery only for a decode-resolved JAL while retaining EX target and misalignment-trap behavior for all control transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the direct-JAL predictor wiring and connect the simplified sequential fetch successor to the existing decode redirect plumbing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add direct-JAL decode-recovery, forwarded adjacent control flow, and misaligned-JAL trap tests covering PC order, RVFI fields, and 