ogs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r1s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-22959/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): An iterative EX divider must preserve the pipeline's valid/retirement progress contract while it holds ID/EX; freezing around a multicycle response can make DIV/REM formal assumptions unreachable and fail liveness even when unrelated instructions pass.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Bounded radix-4 divide pipeline\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cone is paid in every EX-stage\\ntiming analysis even though CoreMark's measured inner loops rarely execute\\ndivision. The earlier 32-cycle replacement confirmed the opportunity but\\nexceeded the bounded formal-retirement window and broke liveness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cone is paid in every EX-stage\\ntiming analysis even though CoreMark's measured inner loops rarely execute\\ndivision. The earlier 32-cycle replacement confirmed the opportunity but\\nexceeded the bounded formal-retirement window and broke liveness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real divide/remainder ALU path with an eight-cycle radix-4\\niterative unit. A precise EX interlock will accept each divide exactly once,\\nallow older MEM/WB work to drain, retain the DIV payload while busy, and\\nadvance one normal EX/MEM result on the fixed completion cycle. Eight cycles\\nkeeps total fetch-to-retire latency within the existing 20-step formal depth,\\nwhile removing the large combinational divider from the ordinary EX critical\\npath. MUL remains combinational and the ALTOPS behavior remains equivalent\\nfor formal checks.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU selection from the normal EX ALU while retaining the formal ALTOPS mapping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an eight-cycle radix-4 signed/unsigned divide unit with quotient/remainder selection and exact RV32M divide-by-zero and overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class operations once, preserve their ID/EX payload during the fixed-latency operation, and emit exactly one completed EX/MEM entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divider-busy interlock that freezes younger stages without suppressing older retirement or duplicate transactions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire divider request, response, and busy state through the in-order pipeline and existing memory-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise exact quotient and remainder results, signed corner cases, and divide-by-zero through the bounded execution path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed retirement-order and forward-progress tests for back-to-back divide operations and divide results consumed by following instructions.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU selection from the normal EX ALU while retaining the formal ALTOPS mapping.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an eight-cycle radix-4 signed/unsigned divide unit with quotient/remainder selection and exact RV32M divide-by-zero and overflow handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class operations once, preserve their ID/EX payload during the fixed-latency operation, and emit exactly one completed EX/MEM entry.\"}, 