icate recovery; load-dependent\\nor misaligned JALRs retain the current EX path so their interlock and trap\\nsemantics stay exact. This changes recovery-stage topology without adding a\\ntarget lookup or return stack to the fetch-critical predictor cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the existing ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID bit without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal, operand-ready, aligned JALR targets with the existing decode bypass network and emit the existing early redirect interface for both branches and JALR.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve JALR link-value and misalignment handling while suppressing EX recovery for a control transfer already redirected in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the generalized decode control redirect through the existing fetch and redirect-priority paths without changing the predictor lookup cone.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain load-use and dmem-stall precedence while treating a decode-resolved JALR exactly like the existing one-slot decode branch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add independent, ALU-forwarded, load-dependent, and misaligned JALR cases covering recovery depth, link writeback, precise traps, and RVFI PC/order sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the existing ID/EX branch-resolved marker into a control-resolved-in-ID bit without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal, operand-ready, aligned JALR targets with the existing decode bypass network and emit 