lect a dedicated same-cycle memory-result forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the sign/zero-extended MEM load result as the youngest forwarding input for rs1 and rs2, including store-data, branch, and JALR operand uses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the MEM-stage bypass result into the EX forwarding network while retaining current dmem-stall priority and RVFI wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Eliminate the fixed load-use bubble while preserving global dmem backpressure holds, redirect precedence, and bubbles for no other reason.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add back-to-back load-to-ALU, load-to-store, load-to-branch, and load-to-JALR tests under ready and delayed dmem responses, checking retirement order and RVFI operands.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish a writing load in EX/MEM from an ALU producer and select a dedicated same-cycle memory-result forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the sign/zero-extended MEM load result as the youngest forwarding input for rs1 and rs2, including store-data, branch, and JALR operand uses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the MEM-stage bypass result into the EX forwarding network while retaining current dmem-stall priority and RVFI wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Eliminate the fixed load-use bubble while preserving global dmem backpressure holds, redirect precedence, and bubbles for no other reason.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add back-to-back load-to-ALU, load-to-store, load-to-branch, and load-to-JALR tests under ready and delayed dmem responses, checking retirement order and RVFI operands.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 229.45, \"delta_pct\": -34.19, \"vs_baseline\": -18.87, \"fmax_mhz\": 90.68, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3952044, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8002, \"ff\": 1936, \"seeds\": [93.77, 87.57, 90.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:37:04.304869Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r8s1 (regression, -34.19%): A same-cycle dmem-to-EX load bypass can lose badly when its read-data extension and forwarding mux extend the dependent ALU timing cone, so removing a CoreMark load-use bubble requires post-route proof that the memory-to-EX path is faster than the saved cycle.\"}\n27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Timing-isolated store write buffer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Random dmem backpressure currently freezes the entire in-order pipe for\\nevery store, even though a completed store has no register result and most\\nfollowing CoreMark work can execute independently. The failed load bypass\\nshows that a same-cycle dmem-to-EX path is too expensive, so stall hiding\\nshould be confined to the store-side memory interface instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Random dmem backpressure currently freezes the entire in-order pipe for\\nevery store, even though a completed store has no register result and most\\nfollowing CoreMark work can execute independently. The failed load bypass\\nshows that a same-cycle dmem-to-EX path is too expensive, so stall hiding\\nshould be confined to the store-side memory interface instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact one-entry, registered write-behind buffer for stores. An\\naccepted store retires normally and enqueues its aligned address, replicated\\ndata, and byte mask without waiting for dmemReady; the buffer alone drives\\nthe request until accepted. Younger loads and stores stop behind a pending\\nstore to preserve ordered memory visibility, while independent ALU and\\ncontrol instructions continue. Registering the buffer request and keeping\\ndmemReady out of fetch and EX control cones should recover isolated store\\nstalls without the placement pressure of a broad front-end queue.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/store_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry registered store queue with valid/empty state, stable aligned request fields, and a drain handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Enqueue legal stores into an empty buffer, retain exact RVFI store fields at retirement, and block loads or a second store while an older write is pending.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace store-side global dmem stalls with buffer-full and ordered-memory interlocks while retaining load-response stalls and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered buffer to dmem pins and expose its occupancy and enqueue status to the pipeline controls without changing the top-level I/O contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized stalled-store tests covering independent progress, load/store ordering, redirects around pending stores, RVFI order, and exact byte-lane data.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/store_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry registered store queue with valid/empty state, stable aligned request fields, and a drain handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Enqueue legal stores into an empty buffer, retain exact RVFI store fields at retirement, and block loads or a second store while an older write is pending.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace store-side global dmem stalls with buffer-fu