y is insufficient when a four-cycle radix-8 divider globally interlocks issue: its per-step arithmetic and stall/response control must be shown cheaper than the removed EX cone and its rare-operation latency on CoreMark.\n  - 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-006-r13s2 (regression, -55.22%): A decode-only indirect-target cache can still lose badly when its valid/tag comparison, 32-bit target mux, and predictor-to-ID routing sit on the ID redirect path; CoreMark's recurring JALRs do not save enough EX recoveries to amortize that control cone.\nhyp-20260711-001-r12s0.yaml\nhyp-20260711-002-r12s1.yaml\nhyp-20260711-003-r12s2.yaml\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
