p-20260711-002-r11s1\tCorrect 30-bit word-PC spine\tregression\t140.48\t\nhyp-20260711-005-r12s1\tRegistered fetch decode boundary\tregression\t372.83\t\nhyp-20260711-005-r13s1\tFormal-safe bounded divider split\tregression\t171.34\t\nhyp-20260711-005-r14s1\tIn-order memory lookahead queue\tbroken\tn/a\tcosim_failed: coremark.elf\nhyp-20260711-002-r4s1\nReplace the combinational IF-to-ID payload with a two-entry, PC-tagged\ninstruction skid queue. Fetch fills an empty queue slot whenever imem is\nready while ID independently consumes the head, allowing a previously\nfetched instruction to enter decode during a later imem stall. Each entry\ncarries its predictor-selected successor so sequential prefetch remains\ncorrect; EX and ID redirects synchronously invalidate younger queued\nentries and restart fetch at the resolved target. This keeps the existing\nsingle-retire pipeline and RVFI boundary intact while converting many\nisolated zero-wait misses into no-bubble cycles.\n\n\nnull\nhyp-20260711-002-r5s1\nInsert a one-entry write buffer between MEM and the dmem pins. A store may\nretire into an empty buffer in one cycle even when dmemReady is low; the\nbuffer holds its aligned address, replicated data, and byte enables until\nthe bus accepts it. Loads and a second store wait until the older buffered\nstore drains, preserving in-order memory visibility, while independent\nALU/control instructions continue through the existing single-retire\npipeline. This converts isolated store-side bus stalls into useful work\nwithout lengthening the predictor lookup or EX arithmetic cone.\n\nnull\nplacement_failed\nhyp-20260711-002-r9s1\nAdd a compact one-entry, registered write-behind buffer for stores. An\naccepted store retires normally and enqueues its aligned address, replicated\ndata, and byte mask without waiting for dmemReady; the buffer alone drives\nthe request until accepted. Younger loads and stores stop behind a pending\nstore to preserve ordered memory visibility, while independent ALU and\ncontrol instructions continue. Registering the buffer request and keeping\ndmemReady out of fetch and EX control cones should recover isolated store\nstalls without the placement pressure of a broad front-end queue.\n\nnull\nformal_failed: reg_ch0\n\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:27  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:27  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:27  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:27  Status: failed\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:28 (28)\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:22 (22)\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\nSBY 14:44:56 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\n\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\nFailed: reg_ch0\n\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 14..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 15..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 16..\nSBY 14:44:29 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping 