f_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a fetch-queue entry bundle containing PC, instruction, predicted successor, and validity metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the combinational IF/ID payload with a two-entry instruction skid queue, imem-ready fill control, and redirect-safe invalidation/restart logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire imem readiness, decode-consume control, and the existing ID/EX redirect priorities into the decoupled fetch front end.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Change instruction-stall control from immediate pipeline bubbling to queue-head availability and preserve precise load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decode-stage consume/hold condition required to pop exactly one queued instruction only when ID/EX can capture it.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed randomized-imem-stall tests for queue fill/drain, branch and JAL redirect flushing, load-use holds, RVFI order, and no duplicate retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 334.25, \"delta_pct\": -2.91, \"vs_baseline\": 18.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.65, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3938669, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 11431, \"ff\": 2123, \"seeds\": [131.13, 131.65, 137.1], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:11:15.845885Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4}\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Folded-PC BHT indexing\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The profitable 16-entry BHT currently indexes only PC[5:2], so branch\\nsites separated by 64-byte code regions can repeatedly overwrite the\\nsame two-bit counter. CoreMark has several small hot routines and loops,\\nmaking destructive direction aliasing a likely remaining source of\\nrecoveries after decode-stage branch resolution.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The profitable 16-entry BHT currently indexes only PC[5:2], so branch\\nsites separated by 64-byte code regions can repeatedly overwrite the\\nsame two-bit counter. CoreMark has several small hot routines and loops,\\nmaking destructive direction aliasing a likely remaining source of\\nrecoveries after decode-stage branch resolution.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the direct BHT index with a four-bit folded-PC hash, for example\\nPC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], for both lookup and resolved-branch training. This\\nretains the existing 16 counters, reset policy, direct B-immediate target\\npath, and JAL behavior, but distributes otherwise congruent branch PCs\\nacross the table. Four local XOR gates should be materially cheaper than\\nanother predictor state array or target lookup, while fewer alias-driven\\ndirection misses improve CoreMark 