rly-resolution optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode stage already compares fully bypassed branch operands and\\ncomputes the direct successor, yet EX repeats the branch comparison and\\ntarget calculation before registering the same RVFI pc_wdata result. This\\nduplicate conditional-control cone adds LUTs and routing to the EX/MEM\\nendpoint after the successful early-resolution optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the decode-stage branch decision authoritative for every legal\\nconditional branch once its operands are ready. Carry the resolved taken\\nbit, successor, and target-misalignment fault state through ID/EX so EX\\nselects the recorded result, trains the BHT from the recorded direction,\\nand preserves precise illegal/trap behavior without recomputing a branch\\ncomparator or PC-plus-immediate adder. This should shorten the EX control\\npath while retaining the existing load interlock and recovery semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with decode-resolved branch direction, successor, and misalignment metadata; remove obsolete EX/MEM branch-only payload fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture the fully bypassed conditional-branch outcome for legal ready branches, including the taken misaligned-target fault condition, alongside the existing early redirect result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace duplicated conditional-branch comparison and target generation with the carried decode result, preserving redirect priority, trap conversion, RVFI pc_wdata, and BHT training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update EX/MEM bundle assumptions after removal of branch-only fields that are no longer consumed downstream.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cases for b