 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 14:54:13 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 14:54:13 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_60 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 14:54:13 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2/formal/last_run-50634.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-terra-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-003-r10s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-50634/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n32:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Prune duplicate decode writeback bypass\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so their bypass muxes participate in\\nthe decode-to-PC recovery cone. The register file is explicitly write-first,\\nbut ID repeats a writeback address comparison and data mux for each branch\\nsource before applying the genuinely necessary MEM and EX bypasses.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID, so their bypass muxes participate in\\nthe decode-to-PC recovery cone. The register file is explicitly write-first,\\nbut ID repeats a writeback address comparison and data mux for each branch\\nsource before applying the genuinely necessary MEM and EX bypasses.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove ID's redundant WB-to-branch operand bypass and its three writeback\\nports. The regfile already returns wb_w_data for a same-cycle matching read\\naddress, making branch_rs1/branch_rs2 identical before the remaining\\nage-prioritized MEM and EX overrides. This eliminates two 5-bit comparators,\\nzero-register tests, and 32-bit mux legs from the early branch-resolution\\ncone, improving Fmax without changing instruction scheduling, IPC, RVFI, or\\nbypass semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the redundant writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the redundant writeback bypass inputs and comparison/mux legs from decode-stage branch operand selection, retaining MEM and EX forwarding priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused writeback-to-ID branch-bypass wiring while retaining the register-file write port and all other pipeline connections.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add a branch whose source register is written in WB during decode, plus EX and MEM override cases, to prove write-first regfile behavior and branch RVFI sequencing remain exact.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 333.04, \"delta_pct\": -5.81, \"vs_baseline\": 17.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 138.16, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7863, \"ff\": 1896, \"seeds\": [142.71, 138.16, 134.34], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:09:47.303217Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 11}\n33:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Correct 30-bit word-PC spine\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The fetch PC, predicted successor, and carried retirement PCs are always\\ninstruction aligned, yet the core routes their invariant low two zero bits\\nand uses 32-bit adders in the timing-sensitive fetch and redirect paths.\\nThe prior word-PC attempt failed cosimulation because it retained an\\nencoded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The fetch PC, predicted successor, and carried retirement PCs are always\\ninstruction aligned, yet the core routes their invariant low two zero bits\\nand uses 32-bit adders in the timing-sensitive fetch and redirect paths.\\nThe prior word-PC attempt failed cosimulation because it retained an\\nencoded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Represent sequential fetch, direct-JAL prediction, conditional-branch\\nrecovery, and non-JALR resolved successors as 30-bit instruction-word\\naddresses. PC+4 becomes pc_word+1. Direct JAL must use exactly the signed\\nJ-immediate bits [31:2], and B targets exactly the signed B-immediate bits\\n[31:2], dropping both encoded invariant low bits; this corrects the failed\\nearlier conversion. Reconstruct byte PCs only at imem, AUIPC/link-data,\\nJALR's full-width target/alignment check, and RVFI boundaries. Narrowing\\nthe persistent PC feedback/routing cone should improve Fmax without adding\\nqueueing state or changing single-retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 140.48, \"delta_pct\": -60.27, \"vs_baseline\": -50.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 58.28, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7923, \"ff\": 1906, \"seeds\": [58.1, 58.28, 61.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:13:43.138227Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Aligned decode-stage JAL steering\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 380.62, \"delta_pct\": 7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7729, \"ff\": 1910, \"seeds\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"predictor\\\") | [.id, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"), .title, (.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"predictor\\\") | [.id, .outcome, (.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"), (.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"), .title, (.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\timprovement\t316.16\t11.79\tCompact direct branch predictor\tAdd a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r2s2\tregression\t308.55\t-2.41\tCommitted return-stack JALR predictor\tExtend the existing direct predictor with a tiny committed return-address\\nstack. Detect canonical RV32 calls and returns in fetch: predict a JALR\\nreturn through the stack top, while EX pushes PC+4 for resolved calls and\\npops only resolved canonical returns. Keeping updates at resolution avoids\\ncorrupting predictor state on a mispredicted speculative path, and avoids\\nthe tags, target RAM, and lookup delay of a general indirect BTB.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r3s2\tregression\t308.36\t-2.47\tCold-start BTFNT branch fallback\tAdd one validity bit per existing BHT entry and use static backward-taken,\\nforward-not-taken prediction only while that entry is untrained. On the\\nfirst resolved branch, mark the entry valid and retain the present two-bit\\nsaturating-counter behavior. This removes cold backward-loop redirects\\nwithout enlarging the target structure or putting a return-stack lookup on\\nthe fetch critical path; trained branches retain dynamic behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r4s2\tregression\t317.51\t-7.77\tFolded-PC BHT indexing\tReplace the direct BHT index with a four-bit folded-PC hash, for example\\nPC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], for both lookup and resolved-branch training. This\\nretains the existing 16 counters, reset policy, direct B-immediate target\\npath, and JAL behavior, but distributes otherwise congruent branch PCs\\nacross the table. Four local XOR gates should be materially cheaper than\\nanother predictor state array or target lookup, while fewer alias-driven\\ndirection misses improve CoreMark IPC.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r5s2\timprovement\t345.35\t0.31\tDecode-stage BHT training\tTrain the existing two-bit BHT directly from the validated, operand-ready\\ndecode-stage branch result and remove the redundant EX-to-predictor training\\npath. This advances counter updates by one cycle without changing BHT size,\\nindexing, reset policy, direct-target generation, or the fetch lookup cone.\\nIt should reduce short-loop and closely spaced alias recovery bubbles while\\npreserving the successful ID-stage redirect and EX fallback behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r6s2\tregression\t338.8\t-1.9\tTaken-biased BHT cold start\tInitialize the existing sixteen two-bit BHT counters to weakly taken\\n(2'b10) instead of weakly not taken (2'b01). This removes the first-taken\\nmisprediction for cold loop back edges with no new state, muxing, PC hash,\\nor fetch-path logic. A first not-taken forward branch still trains the same\\ncounter to weakly not taken after one recovery, retaining normal dynamic\\nbehavior and existing decode-stage training semantics.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r7s2\tregression\t319.82\t-8.26\tDecode-assisted return recovery\tRecognize only canonical returns (JALR x0, x1, 0) in decode and use the\\nexisting EX/MEM/WB bypass network to form the aligned x1 target there. When\\nx1 is ready, redirect fetch one cycle earlier and mark the control transfer\\nresolved so EX preserves its normal RVFI pc_wdata without issuing a duplicate\\nredirect. This is a return-specific late predictor: unlike the prior RAS, it\\nadds no state, tag, or target mux to the fetch-critical BHT lookup cone; unlike\\nthe broad JALR experiment, it leaves calls and arbitrary indirect jumps on the\\nproven EX path. Load-dependent or misaligned returns retain EX resolution and\\nexact trap behavior.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r8s2\timprovement\t353.6\t1.43\tJAL-only fetch predictor\tReplace the conditional two-bit BHT prediction with a minimal direct-JAL\\nfetch predictor: JAL is still sent immediately to its encoded target, but\\nconditional branches always fetch PC+4 and rely on the established\\noperand-ready ID redirect for taken outcomes. Remove BHT state and its\\ndecode-stage training interface. This trades the limited remaining benefit\\nof speculative conditional direction (principally load-dependent branches)\\nfor a shorter, lower-fanout fetch-to-PC path while retaining bubble-free\\ndirect calls and jumps.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r9s2\tregression\t279.44\t-20.97\tClean-register return fast predictor\tAdd a conservative decode-stage fast path only for the exact canonical return\\nencoding `jalr x0, x1, 0` when no older EX or MEM writer targets x1. Its target\\nis the clean regfile x1 value with bit zero cleared, so this path needs neither\\noperand-bypass muxes nor a 32-bit add. If x1 is pending, the target is\\nmisaligned, or the pipeline is stalled, retain normal EX-stage JALR recovery\\nand trap behavior. This can recover common leaf/helper returns without adding\\nstate or lengthening the fetch predictor cone.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r10s2\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\tDecode-resolved direct JAL path\tReplace fetch-stage direct-JAL prediction with a decode-stage direct-JAL\\nredirect that reuses the existing ID redirect priority and target path.\\nJAL has no source dependency, so its legal aligned target can steer the PC\\non the edge that captures the JAL into ID/EX, preserving the current\\nno-bubble control-flow behavior. Carry a decode-resolved control marker to\\nsuppress EX's duplicate JAL recovery; leave misaligned JAL targets on the\\nexisting EX trap path. This removes J-immediate extraction, target addition,\\nand the predictor mux from the fetch-critical path while avoiding the bypass,\\npending-register, and indirect-target logic that made return fast paths lose.\\n\nhyp-20260711-003-r11s2\timprovement\t380.62\t7.64\tAligned decode-stage JAL steering\tReplace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
