k\\nspends substantial time in short counted loops, so correctly predicting\\ntheir backward branches can recover those repeated front-end bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage baseline resolves every conditional branch and JAL in EX,\\nflushing two younger instructions whenever control flow changes. CoreMark\\nspends substantial time in short counted loops, so correctly predicting\\ntheir backward branches can recover those repeated front-end bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small PC-indexed two-bit direction table in the fetch path. For a\\nvalidated conditional branch, use its fetched B-immediate as the direct\\ntarget when the counter predicts taken; predict direct JALs taken as well.\\nCarry the predicted next PC to EX, update the counter on branch resolution,\\nand redirect/flush only when resolved control flow differs from the\\nprediction. JALR remains predict-not-taken, keeping the predictor compact\\nand avoiding a costly indirect-target structure near the Fmax limit.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact PC-indexed two-bit counter predictor that recognizes validated B-type branches and direct JAL targets, and trains on resolved conditional branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend fetch and execute pipeline bundles with the predicted next-PC metadata needed for precise misprediction recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use predictor direction and direct targets to select the speculative next PC while preserving reset, stall, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare resolved control flow against the carried prediction and request a redirect only on a misprediction, while exposing branch-training data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire predictor lookup, execute-stage train