 the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Change BHT reset initialization to weakly taken while retaining the current direct PC index, saturating updates, JAL handling, and decode-stage training interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add reset-state tests for a cold taken branch and a cold not-taken branch, then verify counter transitions, saturation, and unchanged direct JAL prediction.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 338.8, \"delta_pct\": -1.9, \"vs_baseline\": 19.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.55, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10700, \"ff\": 1927, \"seeds\": [137.44, 142.25, 140.55], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T16:45:01.518248Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.90%): With a two-bit BHT already in the fetch path, weakly-taken reset harms CoreMark more through cold forward/not-taken branches and aliases than it saves on first counted-loop back edges, so the weakly-not-taken cold bias is the better default.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:20:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock compares a pending load destination with both\\nraw IF/ID register-field bit slices. Several immediate and no-source RV32I\\nforms encode immediate bits in those slices, so a coincidental match inserts\\na bubble even though the following instruction cannot consume the load.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use interlock compares a pending load destination with both\\nraw IF/ID register-field bit slices. Several immediate and no-source RV32I\\nforms encode immediate bits in those slices, so a coincidental match inserts\\na bubble even though the following instruction cannot consume the load.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Derive conservative rs1/rs2-use qualifiers locally from the fetched opcode\\nin the hazard unit, and gate each load-use comparison with its qualifier.\\nPreserve both-source interlocks for OP, STORE, and BRANCH, rs1 interlocks\\nfor OP-IMM, LOAD, and JALR, and conservatively treat every other encoding as\\nsource-free. This removes false immediate-field alias bubbles without\\nchanging decoder control, forwarding, memory ordering, or retirement.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode conservative opcode-local rs1/rs2 use qualifiers and gate load-use comparisons so immediate and source-free encodings cannot create false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the complete fetched instruction to the hazard unit instead of only its raw rs1 and rs2 bit fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add immediate-alias-after-load cases that must not bubble, alongside OP, STORE, BRANCH, LOAD-address, and JALR dependencies that must still interlock and retire with exact RVFI state.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode conservative opcode-local rs1/rs2 use qualifiers and gate load-use comparisons so immediate and source-free encodings cannot create false stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the complete fetc