file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 380.62, \"delta_pct\": 7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7729, \"ff\": 1910, \"seeds\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Share execute control target adders\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic independently builds the same PC-relative\\ntarget for branches and direct JALs, and builds a second rs1-plus-immediate\\nadder for JALR even though its ALU operation is already ADD. These duplicate\\narithmetic cones consume LUTs and routing at the EX/MEM timing endpoint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX control logic independently builds the same PC-relative\\ntarget for branches and direct JALs, and builds a 