mulation because it retained an\\nencoded halfword immediate bit when converting direct-control offsets, not\\nbecause the reduced-width PC topology is architecturally invalid.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Represent sequential fetch, direct-JAL prediction, conditional-branch\\nrecovery, and non-JALR resolved successors as 30-bit instruction-word\\naddresses. PC+4 becomes pc_word+1. Direct JAL must use exactly the signed\\nJ-immediate bits [31:2], and B targets exactly the signed B-immediate bits\\n[31:2], dropping both encoded invariant low bits; this corrects the failed\\nearlier conversion. Reconstruct byte PCs only at imem, AUIPC/link-data,\\nJALR's full-width target/alignment check, and RVFI boundaries. Narrowing\\nthe persistent PC feedback/routing cone should improve Fmax without adding\\nqueueing state or changing single-retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace carried aligned PC and predicted-successor fields with 30-bit word-PC fields while retaining byte-address reconstruction at architectural boundaries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Store the fetch PC in word units, emit io_imemAddr as {pc_word,2'b00}, and retain redirect-over-stall priority with pc_word+1 sequential advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform direct-JAL prediction in word units using the exact signed J-immediate [31:2] encoding, with no retained halfword bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute decode-resolved conditional branch targets from the exact signed B-immediate [31:2] word displacement while preserving existing operand bypass and trap gating.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use word-PC arithmetic for branch/JAL successors and byte-PC reconstruction for AUIPC/link data; keep JALR full-width until its mandated alignment check completes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate narrowed PC metadata through MEM/WB and materialize byte-addressed RVFI PC values without altering memory-access semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Adapt predictor, redirect, and RVFI wiring to the internal word-PC representation while preserving the external imem and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add forward/backward JAL and branch cases that verify exact word-offset conversion, plus AUIPC, JALR, misalignment, RVFI PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 140.48, \"delta_pct\": -60.27, \"vs_baseline\": -50.33, \"fmax_mhz\": 58.28, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7923, \"ff\": 1906, \"seeds\": [58.1, 58.28, 61.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:13:43.138227Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Aligned decode-stage JAL steering\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 380.62, \"delta_pct\": 7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7729, \"ff\": 1910, \"seeds\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\"}\n37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-006-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Elide sequential predictor metadata\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current best core intentionally predicts only PC+4 in fetch, while\\nlegal conditional branches and direct JALs steer from ID. Nevertheless it\\ntransports a 32-bit predicted-next-PC through IF/ID and ID/EX solely to\\nrepresent that invariant sequential successor, adding wide routing and\\nregister load to the control path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best core intentionally predicts only PC+4 in fetch, while\\nlegal conditional branches and direct JALs steer from ID. Nevertheless it\\ntransports a 32-bit predicted-next-PC through IF/ID and ID/EX solely to\\nrepresent that invariant sequential successor, adding wide routing and\\nregister load to the control path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make the sequential predictor implicit rather than carried metadata.\\nRemove predicted_next_pc from the fetch and ID/EX bundles and eliminate\\nthe standalone predictor wiring. IF advances by its local PC+4 default;\\nID determines whether its already-computed branch/JAL successor differs\\nfrom local PC+4, and EX uses the same local comparison only for unresolved\\nJALR recovery. The existing control_resolved_id marker continues to\\nsuppress duplicate EX redirects. This keeps the proven no-table,\\nno-target-adder fetch policy, but removes a redundant 32-bit pipeline\\npayload and its fanout without weakening alignment, trap, or RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant predicted_next_pc members from IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Retire the standalone always-sequential lookup interface, or reduce it to local sequential-policy documentation if the source file remains.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate the PC+4 sequential successor locally while retaining older-EX and ID redirect priority over stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare decode-resolved branch and JAL successors against local PC+4 instead of carried predictor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"For unresolved JALR recovery, compare the resolved successor with local PC+4; preserve the decode-resolution suppression and all trap paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the obsolete predictor instance and predicted-successor wiring while preserving the external imem, dmem, and RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover sequential fall-through, ID-resolved branch and JAL steering, JALR recovery, redirect-over-stall priority, and RVFI PC sequencing after metadata removal.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant predicted_next_pc members from IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Retire the standalone always-sequential lookup interface, or reduce it to local sequential-policy documentation if the source file remains.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate the PC+4 sequential successor locally while retaining older-EX and ID redirect priority over stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare decode-resolved branch and JAL successors against local PC+4 instead of carried predictor metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"For unresolved JALR recovery, compare the resolved successor with local PC+4; preserve the decode-resolution suppression and all trap paths.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the obsolete predictor instance and predicted-successor wiring while preserving the external imem, dmem, and RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover sequential fall-through, ID-resolved branch and JAL steering, JALR recovery, redirect-over-stall priority, and RVFI PC sequencing after metadata removal.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 186.69, \"delta_pct\": -50.95, \"vs_baseline\": -33.99, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.45, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7762, \"ff\": 1871, \"seeds\": [77.36, 80.31, 77.45], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:07:11.863783Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-006-r12s2 (regression, -50.95%): Even an invariant PC+4 successor is valuable registered metadata: recomputing `in.pc + 4` in both ID and EX redirect comparisons adds 32-bit arithmetic to recovery control cones, so payload elision must not trade routing for repeated critical-path computation without post-route evidence.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
