{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-006-r13s2.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-006-r13s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-006-r13s2\ntitle: \"Decode-stage indirect target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current core resolves direct control flow in decode, but every JALR\n  still waits for EX and flushes younger sequential fetches. Earlier return\n  predictors lost because their RAS, bypass, and target-generation logic was\n  too costly; a trained target lookup can avoid those expensive components.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny PC-indexed indirect-target cache that is looked up only in ID,\n  not on the fetch-to-PC path. A valid cache hit on a legal JALR speculatively\n  redirects via the existing ID redirect port and substitutes the cached\n  successor into the already-carried predicted-next-PC field. EX continues to\n  compute the architectural JALR target, trains only resolved aligned JALRs,\n  and recovers normally on a stale target. This removes recurring JALR\n  recovery bubbles when targets are stable while avoiding an RAS, source\n  bypass network, or target adder in the decode fast path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a very small direct-mapped valid/tag/target cache with decode lookup and EX-stage training ports for resolved aligned JALRs; retain the sequential fetch successor output.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the IF/ID PC lookup and cached target into ID, and pass EX's resolved JALR training event back to the predictor without altering the external buses or RVFI ports.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"On a capturable legal JALR cache hit, issue an ID redirect and capture the cached successor as prediction metadata, while keeping direct branch/JAL resolution and all stall/flush priorities unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose a training event only for valid non-trapping JALR resolution and retain successor-versus-carried-prediction recovery so stale cache entries are corrected precisely.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Test cache reset, hit/miss behavior, PC alias/tag rejection, aligned JALR training, and replacement semantics.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add repeated-JALR hit, stale-target recovery, dmem/imem-stall, misaligned-JALR trap, RVFI-PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
