{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files cores/bench/test | sort && rg -n 'hyp-20260711-003-r8s2|hyp-20260711-003-r11s2|JAL-only fetch predictor|Aligned decode-stage JAL steering' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\ncores/bench/test/test_branch_predictor.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"JAL-only fetch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID with bypassing, so a sequential\\nconditional fetch can usually be repaired at the same edge without an\\nextra decode bubble. The BHT still places a counter-array mux, branch\\nlegality decode, immediate-target adder, and direction mux on every\\ninstruction-fetch path. Direct JALs cannot use the ID branch mechanism\\nand remain worth predicting at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches now resolve in ID with bypassing, so a sequential\\nconditional fetch can usually be repaired at the same edge without an\\nextra decode bubble. The BHT still places a counter-array mux, branch\\nlegality decode, immediate-target adder, and direction mux on every\\ninstruction-fetch path. Direct JALs cannot use the ID branch mechanism\\nand remain worth predicting at fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the conditional two-bit BHT prediction with a minimal direct-JAL\\nfetch predictor: JAL is still sent immediately to its encoded target, but\\nconditional branches always fetch PC+4 and rely on the established\\noperand-ready ID redirect for taken outcomes. Remove BHT state and its\\ndecode-stage training interface. This trades the limited remaining benefit\\nof speculative conditional direction (principally load-dependent branches)\\nfor a shorter, lower-fanout fetch-to-PC path while retaining bubble-free\\ndirect calls and jumps.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the conditional BHT counter array, PC-index lookup, and training ports; retain only validated direct-JAL target prediction with sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete decode-stage BHT training wires and instantiate the simplified JAL-only predictor while preserving predicted-next-PC recovery plumbing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch-training outputs and keep existing operand-ready conditional branch comparison and early redirect behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain direct-JAL speculation and verify that sequential conditional fetch plus ID redirect has the required redirect and stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Replace counter-state tests with direct-JAL and sequential-conditional lookup tests, including reserved branch encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add taken and not-taken conditional branch cases, including forwarded and load-dependent operands, to verify decode recovery, RVFI PC order, and direct-JAL fetch behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the conditional BHT counter array, PC-index lookup, and training ports; retain only validated direct-JAL target prediction with sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete decode-stage BHT training wires and instantiate the simplified JAL-only predictor while preserving predicted-next-PC recovery plumbing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch-training outputs and keep existing operand-ready conditional branch comparison and early redirect behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain direct-JAL speculation and verify that sequential conditional fetch plus ID redirect has the required redirect and stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Replace counter-state tests with direct-JAL and sequential-conditional lookup tests, including reserved branch encodings.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add taken and not-taken conditional branch cases, including forwarded and load-dependent operands, to verify decode recovery, RVFI PC order, and direct-JAL fetch behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 353.6, \"delta_pct\": 1.43, \"vs_baseline\": 25.03, \"fmax_mhz\": 146.69, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8082, \"ff\": 1900, \"seeds\": [147.1, 146.69, 145.29], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:34:38.774222Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r8s2 (improvement, +1.43%): After operand-ready conditional branches redirect in ID, removing the BHT's counter lookup, branch-legality decode, target adder, and direction mux from the fetch-to-PC path can outperform its remaining load-dependent-branch benefit while retaining immediate direct-JAL prediction.\"}\n28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Clean-register return fast predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The JAL-only fetch path has restored Fmax, while conditional branches already\\nrecover in decode. Canonical returns remain a recurring two-slot EX recovery,\\nbut the previous general decode-return path lost heavily to its bypass and\\ntarget-calculation logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The JAL-only fetch path has restored Fmax, while conditional branches already\\nrecover in decode. Canonical returns remain a recurring two-slot EX recovery,\\nbut the previous general decode-return path lost heavily to its bypass and\\ntarget-calculation logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a conservative decode-stage fast path only for the exact canonical return\\nencoding `jalr x0, x1, 0` when no older EX or MEM writer targets x1. Its target\\nis the clean regfile x1 value with bit zero cleared, so this path needs neither\\noperand-bypass muxes nor a 32-bit add. If x1 is pending, the target is\\nmisaligned, or the pipeline is stalled, retain normal EX-stage JALR recovery\\nand trap behavior. This can recover common leaf/helper returns without adding\\nstate or lengthening the fetch predictor cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-resolved canonical return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only jalr x0,x1,0; conservatively require x1 not to be pending in EX or MEM, form the target as the aligned clean regfile value, and issue a decode redirect only for an aligned capturable return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried return-resolved marker to avoid duplicate recovery while retaining full JALR target, link, forwarding, and misalignment-trap behavior for every other case.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow decode return redirect through the existing older-EX redirect priority without changing the JAL-only fetch predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add clean-register canonical-return, pending-x1 fallback, and misaligned-return tests that check redirect timing, RVFI PC/order, link semantics, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename or generalize the carried decode-resolution bit so EX can suppress only a verified decode-resolved canonical return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only jalr x0,x1,0; conservatively require x1 not to be pending in EX or MEM, form the target as the aligned clean regfile value, and issue a decode redirect only for an aligned capturable return.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried return-resolved marker to avoid duplicate recovery while retaining full JALR target, link, forwarding, and misalignment-trap behavior for every other case.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow decode return redirect through the existing older-EX redirect priority without changing the JAL-only fetch predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add clean-register canonical-return, pending-x1 fallback, and misaligned-return tests that check redirect timing, RVFI PC/order, link semantics, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 279.44, \"delta_pct\": -20.97, \"vs_baseline\": -1.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.58, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4136096, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8118, \"ff\": 1898, \"seeds\": [115.58, 118.23, 111.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:47:27.432814Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r9s2 (regression, -20.97%): Even a bypass-free `jalr x0, x1, 0` decode redirect regresses CoreMark when x1-pending comparisons, target alignment gating, and the ID early-redirect selection add control/routing cost that common return bubbles cannot amortize, so canonical-return recovery should remain in EX unless its decode path is demonstrably cheaper post-route.\"}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Aligned decode-stage JAL steering\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current JAL-only predictor avoids direct-JAL recovery bubbles, but it\\nstill places J-immediate extraction and a 32-bit PC-relative target adder\\non every fetch-to-PC feedback path. Conditional branches already redirect\\nfrom decode without a bubble when their result is safe to capture.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the fetch-stage direct-JAL target prediction with a verified\\ndecode-stage JAL redirect. Fetch remains sequential, while a legal JAL\\nwhose target is instruction aligned steers the PC on the same edge that\\ncaptures it into ID/EX. Carry a one-bit captured-resolution marker so EX\\nrecomputes the architectural successor for RVFI but never performs a\\nduplicate redirect. Misaligned JAL targets, older EX recovery, stalls, and\\nflushes retain their existing EX-stage behavior. This removes the JAL\\nimmediate adder and selection mux from the Fmax-critical fetch loop without\\nadding return prediction, branch-table state, or decode operand bypassing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Reduce lookup to the sequential successor so no J-immediate extraction or target adder remains on the fetch prediction path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a direct-JAL decode redirect only when the instruction is valid, legal, aligned, capturable, and not superseded by the existing flush or stall controls; set a resolution marker only under that same gate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Generalize the ID/EX decode-resolution marker from conditional branches to aligned decode-resolved direct control flow without widening the carried successor payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep full JAL target and misalignment computation for architectural pc_next and traps, but suppress recovery solely for the captured decode-resolved marker.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the sequential predictor and decode JAL redirect through the existing older-EX-wins redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add aligned forward and backward JAL steering tests plus stall, older-redirect, and misaligned-JAL cases that check retirement order, RVFI PCs, link writes, and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 380.62, \"delta_pct\": 7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 34.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 157.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7729, \"ff\": 1910, \"seeds\": [165.4, 135.81, 157.9], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:23.476499Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r11s2 (improvement, +7.64%): Once ID can capture a legal aligned JAL and carry a resolution marker to suppress EX recovery, moving its immediate target adder out of the fetch-to-PC loop improves CoreMark timing without sacrificing architectural successor or misalignment handling.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
