ves recurring JALR\\nrecovery bubbles when targets are stable while avoiding an RAS, source\\nbypass network, or target adder in the decode fast path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped valid/tag/target cache with decode lookup and EX-stage training ports for resolved aligned JALRs; retain the sequential fetch successor output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID PC lookup and cached target into ID, and pass EX's resolved JALR training event back to the predictor without altering the external buses or RVFI ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"On a capturable legal JALR cache hit, issue an ID redirect and capture the cached successor as prediction metadata, while keeping direct branch/JAL resolution and all stall/flush priorities unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a training event only for valid non-trapping JALR resolution and retain successor-versus-carried-prediction recovery so stale cache entries are corrected precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test cache reset, hit/miss behavior, PC alias/tag rejection, aligned JALR training, and replacement semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add repeated-JALR hit, stale-target recovery, dmem/imem-stall, misaligned-JALR trap, RVFI-PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped valid/tag/target cache with decode lookup and EX-stage training ports for resolved aligned JALRs; retain the sequential fetch successor output.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the IF/ID PC lookup and cached target into ID, and pass EX's resolved JALR training event back to the predictor without altering the external buses or RVFI ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"On a capturable legal JALR cache hit, issue an ID redirect and capture the cached successor as prediction metadata, while keeping direct branch/JAL resolution and all stall/flush priorities unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a training event only for valid non-trapping JALR resolution and retain successor-versus-carried-prediction recovery so stale cache entries are corrected precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_branch_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Test cache reset, hit/miss behavior, PC alias/tag rejection, aligned JALR training, and replacement semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add repeated-JALR hit, stale-target recovery, dmem/imem-stall, misaligned-JALR trap, RVFI-PC, and retirement-order coverage.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 170.46, \"delta_pct\": -55.22, \"vs_baseline\": -39.73, \"fmax_mhz\": 70.54, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4138267, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8411, \"ff\": 2144, \"seeds\": [68.33, 70.54, 75.38], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:25:49.070088Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-006-r13s2 (regression, -55.22%): A decode-only indirect-target cache can still lose badly when its valid/tag comparison, 32-bit target mux, and predictor-to-ID routing sit on the ID redirect path; CoreMark's recurring JALRs do not save enough EX recoveries to amortize that control cone.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r14s0\", \"title\": \"Right-size independent RV32 multipliers\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU builds three multiply products on every cycle after explicitly\\nextending both RV32 operands to 64 bits. This can infer oversized multiplier\\ncones and unnecessarily consume LUT/routing resources near the EX endpoint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU builds three multiply products on every cycle after explicitly\\nextending both RV32 operands to 64 bits. This can infer oversized multiplier\\ncones and unnecessarily consume LUT/routing resources near the EX endpoint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the current independent signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\\nsigned-unsigned product topology, but express each product with native\\n32-bit operands and a 64-bit result. Unlike the prior single shared\\nmultiplier experiment, this avoids an operation-selected operand-extension\\nmux and its control fanout on the multiplier inputs. The narrower fixed\\nproducts preserve every MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU bit result while reducing\\narithmetic width and placement pressure, which should raise Fmax without\\nchanging pipeline timing or CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the explicit 64-bit operand extensions feeding mul_ss, mul_uu, and mul_su with correctly typed native RV32 signed/unsigned operands while retaining separate fixed product cones, result-half selection, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact directed and randomized MUL-family vectors covering negative operands, sign-mixed MULHSU, and all-one unsigned inputs to verify every high and low result half after operand-width tightening.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the explicit 64-bit operand extensions feeding mul_ss, mul_uu, and mul_su with correctly typed native RV32 signed/unsigned operands while retaining separate fixed product cones, result-half selection, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact directed and randomized MUL-family vectors covering negative operands, sign-mixed MULHSU, and all-one unsigned inputs to verify every high and low result half after operand-width tightening.\"}], \"outcome\": \"placement_failed\", \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": \"placement_failed\", \"seeds\": [null, null, null], \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:42:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-005-r14s1\", \"title\": \"In-order memory lookahead queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The CoreMark cosimulation injects approximately 22% dmem backpressure,\\nwhile the current EX/MEM register freezes fetch, decode, and execute for\\nevery pending load or store. CoreMark is load/store dense, so this converts\\nmany independent ALU and control slots into bubbles even though retirement\\nneed not be reordered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The CoreMark cosimulation injects approximately 22% dmem backpressure,\\nwhile the current EX/MEM register freezes fetch, decode, and execute for\\nevery pending load or store. CoreMark is load/store dense, so this converts\\nmany independent ALU and control slots into bubbles even though retirement\\nneed not be reordered.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the single EX/MEM holding point with a compact two-entry in-order\\nexecution-to-memory queue. The head alone owns the dmem request and waits\\nfor its response, while one younger independent instruction may enter the\\ntail and retain its completed EX result. Commit remains strictly head-first\\ninto MEM/WB, so RVFI retirement order and memory visibility remain exactly\\nin order. A conservative pending-load scoreboard stalls only instructions\\nthat read an unresolved load destination; forwarding from completed queued\\nALU entries preserves ordinary dependent ALU chains. This hides isolated\\ndmem stalls without placing predictor lookup, instruction fetch, or ALU\\narithmetic behind a new ready/valid feedback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a compact queued execution-result entry and carry the existing EX/MEM architectural/RVFI metadata through the bounded in-order queue.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_mem_queue.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-entry head-first queue that accepts EX results, presents only its oldest memory operation to dmem, and retires entries only in program order.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce enqueue-ready EX results and select conservative forwarding from completed queued non-load writers without allowing an unresolved load result to be consumed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the queue head, hold a stalled memory request stable, form load data on acceptance, and emit one ordered MEM/WB payload with unchanged RVFI memory fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace global dmem freezing with queue-capacity and unresolved-load dependency interlocks while retaining precise load-use, redirect, and imem-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire queue enqueue/dequeue state, memory ownership, forwarding, and the existing single-channel RVFI retirement boundary without changing top-level ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized dmem-stall tests for independent lookahead, queued ALU forwarding, pending-load dependencies, store/load ordering, redirects, and exact RVFI order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a compact queued execution-result entry and carry the existing EX/MEM architectural/RVFI metadata through the bounded in-order queue.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_mem_queue.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-entry head-first queue that accepts EX results, presents only its oldest memory operation to dmem, and retires entries only in program order.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce enqueue-ready EX results and select conservative forwarding from completed queued non-load writers without allowing an unresolved load result to be consumed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the queue head, hold a stalled memory request stable, form load data on acceptance, and emit one ordered MEM/WB payload with unchanged RVFI memory fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace global dmem freezing with queue-capacity and unresolved-load dependency interlocks while retaining precise load-use, redirect, and imem-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire queue enqueue/dequeue state, memory ownership, forwarding, and the existing single-channel RVFI retirement boundary without changing top-level ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add randomized dmem-stall tests for independent lookahead, queued ALU forwarding, pending-load dependencies, store/load ordering, redirects, and exact RVFI order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-006-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Load-dependent branch direction rescue\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Operand-ready conditional branches and aligned direct JALs already steer in\\ndecode, leaving load-dependent conditional branches as the meaningful\\nrecurring control-flow bubble. The current sequential policy stalls one\\ncycle before such a branch can be resolved in decode.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Operand-ready conditional branches and aligned direct JALs already steer in\\ndecode, leaving load-dependent conditional branches as the meaningful\\nrecurring control-flow bubble. The current sequential policy stalls one\\ncycle before such a branch can be resolved in decode.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny weakly-not-taken, PC-indexed two-bit direction table that is\\nconsulted only when a legal conditional branch is blocked by a matching\\nload in EX. On a taken prediction, capture that branch into ID/EX without\\nthe normal load-use bubble and steer fetch to its already-formed B-immediate\\ntarget; EX forwards the completed load, resolves the architectural outcome,\\ntrains the table, and recovers on a miss. All operand-ready branches retain\\ntheir proven decode-resolution path, and fetch remains the existing simple\\nsequential predictor, so the BHT never extends the fetch-to-PC timing cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small reset-to-weakly-not-taken PC-indexed two-bit table with decode lookup and EX-resolved training ports, while retaining the PC+4 fetch successor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize the exact matching-load branch interlock, use a taken table result to capture the branch and redirect to its direct target, and carry that speculative successor without marking the branch decode-resolved.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress the ordinary one-cycle load-use bubble only for the explicitly predicted-taken conditional-branch case; preserve all other load, bus-stall, and older-redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve and expose a training event for speculative load-dependent branches after normal MEM/WB forwarding, and retain successor comparison so not-taken or stale predictions recover precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the dependency-qualified predictor lookup, EX training event, and exi