{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/core.yaml && rg -n \\\"rtl|store_buffer|mem_stage|core\\\\.sv\\\" cores/bench Makefile formal/run_all.sh\"","aggregated_output":"name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 142.82\n  lut4: 10518\n  ff: 1927\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260711-002-r3s1\n  updated: '2026-07-11T13:44:56.396207Z'\nformal/run_all.sh:26:  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\nformal/run_all.sh:120:# Stage rtl + wrapper + the chosen checks config under the framework's\nformal/run_all.sh:125:# deletes a module in rtl/ leaves a ghost copy in $CORE_DIR from the\nformal/run_all.sh:128:# right to rename/delete files in rtl/, so this cleanup is required.\nformal/run_all.sh:133:# Stage checks.cfg with [verilog-files] auto-derived from actual rtl/\nformal/run_all.sh:137:# files in rtl/. Hardcoding silently fails on those restructurings (or\nMakefile:62:  RTL_DIR    := cores/$(TARGET)/rtl\nMakefile:77:\t@echo \"  make lint TARGET=v1     — verilator lint over cores/<TARGET>/rtl/*.sv\"\nMakefile:94:# -Wno-MULTITOP: until phase 2's core.sv lands and instantiates everything,\nMakefile:95:# rtl/ legitimately has multiple top modules. Drop this once phase 2 is in.\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv:1:// rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv:1:// rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv:18:module mem_stage (\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv:31:  // for downstream RVFI use; mem_stage only consumes a subset, so the\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv:1:// rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:1:// rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv:1:// rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:1:// rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:193:  mem_stage u_mem (\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv:1:// rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:1:// rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:1:// rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:1:// rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:1:// rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/branch_predictor.sv:1:// rtl/branch_predictor.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv:1:// rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv:1:// rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Prune dead EX branch payload\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The placed baseline's critical endpoint is in the EX/MEM register path.\\nEX computes and registers branch_taken and branch_target even though no\\nlater stage consumes either field and RVFI receives pc_next instead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the dead branch_taken and branch_target fields from ex_mem_t and\\ntheir EX-stage calculations/register assignments. This removes an always-on\\nduplicate PC-plus-immediate adder, 33 flip-flops, and its routed EX endpoint\\nwhile preserving redirect behavior and the RVFI pc_wdata path. The smaller\\nEX cone should improve Tang Nano 20K Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused branch_taken and branch_target members from the EX/MEM pipeline bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop registering the dead branch payload while retaining branch condition, redirect, and pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Update the EX/MEM bundle documentation and lint annotations after removing its unused branch payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Retain or add directed branch and jump retirement checks so the optimized EX payload still produces correct pc_wdata and redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 302.55, \"delta_pct\": 6.98, \"vs_baseline\": 6.98, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [135.89, 140.96, 130.68], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:13.260931Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative divide execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed critical path runs through the EX combinational arithmetic\\nnetwork, where fully combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic is present on\\nevery instruction. CoreMark's divide instructions occur in setup and\\nadaptive timing code, not in its measured iteration loop, so paying this\\nFmax cost continuously is unnecessary.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divider/remainder datapaths with a dedicated\\n32-cycle restoring divider execution unit. MUL-family operations retain\\nthe FPGA DSP-backed combinational path; a divide request freezes younger\\npipeline state, then injects the exact quotient or remainder into EX/MEM\\nwhen the unit completes. This removes the long divider cone from ordinary\\nEX timing while keeping RV32M corner cases and RVFI retirement intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal ALU and retain only the ALTOPS formal behavior where required.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with quotient/remainder selection and explicit divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch divide-class ALU operations to the divider, hold their EX payload until response, and emit one normal EX/MEM result on completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an MDU-busy interlock that freezes fetch/decode and preserves retirement ordering while a divide is in flight.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divider request/response and busy interlock into the existing in-order pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M divide and remainder corner-case coverage against the new execution path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: insn_div_ch0\\nine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_sw_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Status: passed\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:02 (2)\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY  9:53:26 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY  9:53:26 